{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JVoaD9Hu2TAV2EtZxwy4sa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora — implementation notes\n2\t\n3\tTactical questions and observations from implementation. Strategic decisions\n4\tare in `C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\notes\\skills-and-agent-tips\\NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md §17`.\n5\t\n6\t## Resolved\n7\t\n8\t### P2 (skills sweep against a single seed) — 2026-05-15\n9\t\n10\tEnd-to-end pipeline working: scout → quarantine → static_screener → embedder\n11\t→ librarian → exec summary. Validated against the 8 Anthropic-shipped skills\n12\tat `C:\\Users\\john\\AppData\\Roaming\\Claude\\local-agent-mode-sessions\\skills-plugin\\...`\n13\t(used as a stand-in for `github.com/anthropics` while we're still in P2 — kind\n14\t`local_mount` in seed_map; P3 wires in HTTP/GitHub scouts).\n15\t\n16\t**Outcomes**\n17\t- 8 fetched → 7 screened → 7 embedded → 7 filed\n18\t- Library index at `library/index.md`; per-skill pages at `library/skills/<slug>/index.md`\n19\t- First exec summary at `reports/skills/<YYYY-MM-DD>/summary.md` with budget block\n20\t- Costs recorded in the `costs` table (vendor='local' / $0 in offline mode)\n21\t\n22\t**One screener rejection (expected, not a bug):**\n23\tThe `schedule` SKILL.md has a description containing unquoted double-quotes —\n24\te.g. `description: Create or update a scheduled task ... users says things like \"every day\"...`\n25\t— which trips strict YAML. The screener correctly flags it. Two paths to take\n26\tin P3: (a) loosen the parser to handle this case; (b) report it as a finding\n27\tfor the upstream skill author. Recommend (b) — strict YAML keeps us safer.\n28\t\n29\t### P2 sandbox / API constraints\n30\t- The Cowork bash sandbox can't reach `api.anthropic.com` directly — its SSL\n31\t  proxy presents a self-signed cert that breaks the Anthropic client. The\n32\t  orchestrator detects this, falls back to a deterministic keyword-based\n33\t  offline embedder, and records cost rows with `vendor='local'` so the budget\n34\t  plumbing is still exercised. Toggle with `AURORA_OFFLINE=1`.\n35\t- On the user's Windows host, the API is reachable; the embedder uses real\n36\t  Claude Haiku and records `vendor='anthropic'`.\n37\t\n38\t### SQLite on Cowork mount\n39\tSQLite locking is unsupported on the host-filesystem mount inside Cowork's\n40\tLinux sandbox. The orchestrator stages to `/tmp` then copies back on close.\n41\tOn Windows, the direct path works and the fallback never triggers.\n42\t\n43\t### `__pycache__` clearing\n44\tThe mount refuses unlink, so stale `.pyc` files would normally trip us. We\n45\tredirect Python's cache to `/tmp` via `PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX` so Python ignores\n46\tthe local `__pycache__/` entirely. On Windows this is unnecessary.\n47\t\n48\t## How to run on Windows (live, with real API)\n49\t\n50\t```powershell\n51\tcd C:\\dev\\aurora\n52\tpython -m venv .venv\n53\t.\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1\n54\tpip install -e .\n55\t# .env should already contain ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (and ideally GEMINI_API_KEY for Critic B)\n56\tpython -m aurora.orchestrator --sweep skills --no-swarm\n57\t```\n58\t\n59\tExpected: ~$0.03–0.05 of Haiku spend, the same 7 skills filed but with real\n60\tLLM-chosen domain/complexity placements (probably similar to the offline\n61\tkeyword ones).\n62\t\n63\t### Session — 2026-05-18 (overnight diagnosis + hardening + cross-runtime HH)\n64\t\n65\t**Overnight outage triaged.** A wmiprvse-driven reboot at 2026-05-16 18:43 had\n66\tsilently killed the in-flight skills sweep. Root cause not in our code — the\n67\tAurora tasks didn't have `WakeToRun` set, so once Windows decided to reboot,\n68\tnothing here was resilient to it. Tasks 16/17/18 (last night's runs) all\n69\tcompleted `ok` once the hardening below was in place.\n70\t\n71\t**Hardening pass applied:**\n72\t\n73\t- All four Aurora scheduled tasks now have `WakeToRun=True` and\n74\t  `StartWhenAvailable=True`, so they recover from missed wake-ups.\n75\t- Active Hours pinned to **04:00–22:00** with `ScheduledInstallTime=3` (a 03:00\n76\t  reboot window) — admin-pushed registry settings at\n77\t  `HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\WindowsUpdate\\UX\\Settings` and\n78\t  `HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\WindowsUpdate\\AU`. This puts\n79\t  the OS reboot squarely between the 01:00 agents-sweep finish and the\n80\t  04:00 quiet window — well clear of all Aurora windows.\n81\t- `publisher.py`: load_dotenv at module top, flush=True on all prints,\n82\t  `_find_git()` helper for non-PATH installs, `_redact_remote()` PAT redactor,\n83\t  `last_push.log` writer for after-the-fact diagnostics.\n84\t- `static_screener._lenient_front_matter`: was using regex position spans\n85\t  (which produced empty captures for some indented blocks → fixture-slug bug\n86\t  where files were placed under e.g.\n87\t  `c-dev-aurora-fixtures-sample-tools-mcp-filesystem-skill-md`); now uses\n88\t  `m.group(2)` directly with continuation-line gobble.\n89\t- `morning_briefing.py`: added missed-run watchdog (>30h since last run for a\n90\t  sweep ⇒ alert in the briefing) and a recurring nudge to swap in the\n91\t  dedicated `aurora` / `aurora-critic-b` API keys until\n92\t  `C:\\dev\\aurora\\.keys-dedicated` exists.\n93\t\n94\t**Helping Hand published to all three runtimes:**\n95\t\n96\t- **Claude Code:** installed at `~/.claude/skills/helping-hand/` +\n97\t  `~/.claude/mcp-servers/aurora-kb/server.py` (FastMCP, official `mcp` SDK).\n98\t  `.mcp.json` points `AURORA_KB_PATH` at the published snapshot.\n99\t- **Gemini CLI:** skill descriptor at `~/.gemini/skills/helping-hand/`. MCP\n100\t  side is best-effort pending Gemini CLI's MCP-stdio maturity (noted in the\n101\t  collaborator setup doc).\n102\t- **Cowork:** `helping-hand.plugin` (6825 B) sits at `C:\\dev\\aurora\\` and is\n103\t  now also pushed to the repo. User installs by dragging into Cowork chat —\n104\t  pending user action.\n105\t\n106\t**Repo publishing wired end-to-end:**\n107\t\n108\t- `https://github.com/johncliechty/aurora-library.git` has tag `20260518`\n109\t  pointing at commit `63d240f \"nightly 20260518\"`. Push log at\n110\t  `_publish/last_push.log`.\n111\t- Two publisher bugs found and fixed in this session:\n112\t  1. `copy_helping_hand_plugin()` candidate list missed `C:\\dev\\aurora\\` so\n113\t     `helping-hand.plugin` wasn't being staged → `git add` aborted on the\n114\t     missing path → empty commit → nothing pushed (silent failure, easy to\n115\t     miss). Now checks `ROOT/helping-hand.plugin` first.\n116\t  2. `git_publish` would `git add` the whole allowlist even if some paths\n117\t     didn't exist (one missing path = nothing staged). Now filters\n118\t     `present = [p for p in SYNC_ALLOWLIST if (PUBLISH_ROOT/p).exists()]`\n119\t     and logs `missing` to `last_push.log`.\n120\t  3. Tag-push now uses `+refs/tags/<tag>` so same-day re-runs cleanly\n121\t     force-update the tag at origin.\n122\t\n123\t- `run-morning-briefing.cmd` now calls publisher after the briefing, so the\n124\t  morning 8:30 task closes the loop — briefing → publish → done.\n125\t\n126\t**Plan reconciliation.** `NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md` advanced to v4 with §18\n127\t(post-deploy status + gaps), §19 (GWL/OpenClaw integration scope, deferred\n128\tto a Cowork session inside `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home`), §20 (this-week punch\n129\tlist). Plan stays curator-side; collaborators see `COLLABORATOR-SETUP.md` in\n130\tthe repo instead.\n131\t\n132\t## Open\n133\t\n134\t- **Dedicated API keys with caps** (§13). Once swapped, run\n135\t  `New-Item C:\\dev\\aurora\\.keys-dedicated -ItemType File` to silence the\n136\t  morning nudge.\n137\t- **Sunburst library map** (`library/_map.html`) — d3 sunburst over\n138\t  domain × complexity, ~80 lines. In §20 punch list.\n139\t- **Neural plasticity scoring for 55 agents** — `neural_plasticity` table\n140\t  population (~$0.10 of Haiku). In §20 punch list.\n141\t- **Template detection heuristic** in `static_screener` — current run treats\n142\t  every artifact as skill/tool/agent (template count stays at 0).\n143\t- **Re-embed legacy URL-slug entries** that pre-date the fixture-slug fix.\n144\t- **Critic B (Gemini) prompt tuning** to reduce Haiku-fallback rate.\n145\t- **HH threshold calibration** after a week of collaborator usage.\n146\t- **GWL/OpenClaw integration** — open a fresh Cowork session inside\n147\t  `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home` and use that workspace's `AGENTS.md` skill resolution\n148\t  order. Plan §19 has the scope notes.\n149\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019yinPhBqtj4zz7WeVeNdaj","session_id":"0e9f13f6-4032-41a4-8d9f-b9e18c221609","uuid":"29ccf08f-4b57-45ee-aabc-436509bf411b","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:39:32.818Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore Aurora revamp + strategy"}
