{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013Bqejt9THudPGtFMgyXZtS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Crucible Stage 0 — Intake & Framing: Aurora Awareness Revamp\n2\t\n3\t**Run:** 2026-06-11. **Mode:** brownfield-on-existing-data. **Substrate:** subscription + Node engine.\n4\t**Inputs:** `docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/HANDOFF.md`, `docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/RESEARCH.md` (adversarially validated).\n5\t**This is the LOCK gate.** Nothing is planned until you lock §1. Drift detection begins after the lock.\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## 1. NORTH STAR — to be LOCKED verbatim (HANDOFF §1, John's intent)\n10\t\n11\t> Aurora exists to **make John aware of all current advances in agentic AI** — agentic\n12\t> systems, theories, approaches, advances in **harnesses**, the **models** that feed them,\n13\t> the **benchmarks**, and new **skills / templates / tools** — serving THREE co-equal jobs:\n14\t> (1) **educate John**, (2) **guide his generation of new agents**, (3) **feed the agentic\n15\t> systems + Claude + Gemini via the Helping Hand retrieval skill.**\n16\t>\n17\t> **Drift guard:** every proposed surface or collection change must serve **awareness +\n18\t> adoption-decision + agent-feeding**. A prettier ops console or richer taxonomy that does\n19\t> not make John *more aware and better-decided* is bloat (fails the inclusion test).\n20\t\n21\t### North-Star success criteria (the measurable spine — every wave must serve ≥1)\n22\t- **NS1 — Awareness:** John can see, per category (skills/tools/templates/agents/**models**),\n23\t  \"what is current best-in-class + what newly moved + why it matters\" without leaving his\n24\t  morning report / a glance at one surface.\n25\t- **NS2 — Model+benchmark intelligence:** the 352 already-collected priced models are\n26\t  surfaced, and at least a thin slice of benchmarks is collected and joined — answering\n27\t  \"which model for X, at what price/perf\" as a decision.\n28\t- **NS3 — Adoption decision:** candidate skills/tools/agents reach John as a fast,\n29\t  trustworthy *should-I-adopt?* decision (summary/risks/advantages/why/effort), and accepted\n30\t  ones feed Helping Hand.\n31\t- **NS4 — Right collection:** the nightly spend buys frontier-relevant agentic-AI items\n32\t  (harnesses/models/benchmarks/high-signal skills-tools-templates), **without losing recall\n33\t  on the obscure small-author find.**\n34\t- **NS5 — Honest value:** John gets a plain-English, no-vanity answer to \"is this working and\n35\t  worth its dollar,\" with sample sizes shown and rates suppressed when ground truth is too thin.\n36\t\n37\t---\n38\t\n39\t## 2. Brownfield ingest — what exists, labeled (Confirmed / Inferred / Gap)\n40\t\n41\t**Reuse, don't rebuild** (AuroraTwo verdict + your constraint):\n42\t- **[Confirmed]** Read-only dashboard package `dashboard/` (blueprint-mountable), `aurora_dashboard.py`, port 5001. Shipped 2026-06-11.\n43\t- **[Confirmed]** `kb/aurora.db`: `artifacts`, `models` (352 rows, all priced), `model_benchmarks` (**0 rows**), `embeddings.domain_path`, `link_health`, `hh_events`, `costs`, `runs`.\n44\t- **[Confirmed]** `reports/` (morning briefing — John: \"fine\"), `helping-hand-plugin/` (KB MCP), `docs/INTEREST_PROFILE.md`, `roles/taste.py` (interest_score on ~30 finds + heuristic fallback).\n45\t- **[Confirmed]** Nightly sweeps real schedule 01:07–06:47; publisher pushes scrubbed snapshot to `aurora-library`.\n46\t- **[Confirmed, from RESEARCH §B]** `hh_events`: 106 events, only **n=7 carry a decision** (6 loaded, 1 dismissed), 21 queries / 10 sessions / 3 weeks. → metrics ground truth is near-zero; learned signals run open-loop.\n47\t- **[Confirmed]** `models` has junk rows (`-1000000` price sentinel; `$0` rows).\n48\t- **[Inferred]** Per-sweep deltas (\"what was new\") already computed/stored (dashboard W4) → promotable to a momentum view cheaply.\n49\t- **[Gap]** No benchmark collection. No model surface. No actionable adoption queue. No human-readable value/health. No relationship map John wants. Collection skewed to arxiv (8 papers / 0 skills-tools-agents last night).\n50\t\n51\t---\n52\t\n53\t## 3. Scope (the §4 deltas, as framed for planning) — IN, OUT, CONSTRAINED\n54\t\n55\t**IN scope (serves NS1–NS5):**\n56\t1. **Model-intelligence surface** — surface the 352 rows; price/performance (intelligence-vs-cost) frontier; \"best-for-X\" cards; sortable master table; junk-filter. *(NS1, NS2 — RESEARCH \"protect\" item; highest value-per-effort.)*\n57\t2. **Benchmark collection (thin slice)** — OpenRouter `/models` (specs/pricing) + Epoch AI CC-BY (GPQA/SWE-bench/FrontierMath); compute own composite; per-cell `source`/`as_of`/`self_reported`. *(NS2.)*\n58\t3. **Collection retargeting** — add high-signal agentic sources (HF Daily Papers, GitHub star-velocity, provider feeds, trusted aggregators) + a frontier-relevance ranker, **with a raw-arxiv recall safety net + authority-bypass lane + label-validated weights.** *(NS4.)*\n59\t4. **Adoption decision surface** — decision-card content (what/fit/recommendation+confidence/advantages/risks/provenance/effort), persisted decisions table feeding Helping Hand — **delivered primarily through the report**, not a heavy daily triage UI. *(NS3.)*\n60\t5. **Honest value + plain-English health** — RAG + 4-question summary; metric set with n shown and rates suppressed below n<30. *(NS5.)*\n61\t6. **Per-category \"what moved + why it matters\" awareness view** (momentum), promoting existing sweep deltas. *(NS1.)*\n62\t7. **Knowledge/relationship map** — LAST, OPTIONAL, **off the ingestion critical path**: PCA/TruncatedSVD + plain canvas (NOT UMAP/numba), non-authoritative. *(NS1 — down-weighted per RESEARCH §B.)*\n63\t\n64\t**OUT of scope (this run):** rebuilding the dashboard package or KB schema; a separate \"critical-analysis tool\" (your later session); any auto consensus \"ring\"; a swarm-harness AuroraTwo rebuild; live cloud viz services.\n65\t\n66\t**CONSTRAINED (hard rules, from you + RESEARCH §B — carried to every wave):**\n67\t- Dirty working tree **IS production**; changes are live. Real schedule 01:07–06:47.\n68\t- **Never** run the `migrate_to_kind_paper` delete step. **Never** read `.env`.\n69\t- KB is **read-only except** the new `decisions` / `feedback` (and benchmark/score) tables.\n70\t- OpenRouter = **transient enrichment**, not redistribution (ToS) — store derived facts, attribute, tolerate 401.\n71\t- **Per-row benchmark license metadata** (Epoch CC-BY; Aider/Terminal-Bench Apache-2.0; MMLU-Pro absent from Epoch).\n72\t- **No metric rate shown below n<30**; show raw counts; name the open-loop/bootstrap state.\n73\t- **UMAP/numba/llvmlite must NOT be on the nightly ingestion critical path** (isolate, or use PCA+canvas).\n74\t- `frontier_score` weights **validated against John's labeled liked/rejected finds** before any gate is trusted; authority-bypass lane preserves recall.\n75\t\n76\t---\n77\t\n78\t## 4. Inclusion test + Oranges foresight (receipt)\n79\t\n80\t**Inclusion test applied now:** the knowledge map (item 7) is the weakest North-Star server (RESEARCH: \"least decision-useful; same class John rejected\") — it survives only because John explicitly asked for it AND it's fenced to optional/off-critical-path. Everything else maps directly to NS1–NS5.\n81\t\n82\t**Oranges foresight (real-intent, 2-3 steps ahead):**\n83\t- **Real goal behind \"am I wasting a dollar a night?\"** is not a cost report — it's *trust that the spend buys awareness he'd otherwise miss.* So value-accounting (NS5) and right-collection (NS4) are load-bearing, not cosmetic.\n84\t- **Reorder receipt:** model-intelligence (already-paid-for data) is sequenced FIRST despite the handoff listing surfaces and collection co-equally — counterfactual cost of not doing so: we'd spend the first wave on collection plumbing while the highest-value, zero-new-data win keeps sitting invisible.\n85\t- **Dropped branch:** a daily keyboard-triage adoption queue — counterfactual cost: ~2 decisions/week don't justify a visit-me surface; mitigated by moving the decision into the report (where John already is), preserving the value while dropping the build.\n86\t- **Cross-cutting win surfaced early:** push value into the **morning report / a weekly email**, not new surfaces John must visit — this threads through NS1/NS3/NS5.\n87\t\n88\t---\n89\t\n90\t## 🚦 LOCK GATE — your decision\n91\t\n92\t**To proceed to Stage 1 (Master Plan), please confirm:**\n93\t\n94\t1. **Lock the North Star** in §1 (and its NS1–NS5 success criteria) as the frozen objective? (yes / edit)\n95\t2. **Scope §3** — anything to ADD, CUT, or move between IN / OUT / CONSTRAINED? (In particular: keep the knowledge map IN-but-optional, or cut it entirely this run?)\n96\t3. **Any constraint missing** from §3's hard-rules list?\n97\t\n98\tNothing downstream is planned until you lock. After the lock, Stage 1 runs the Oranges brainstorm + Shark-Tank loop to a phased Master Plan, presented to you verbatim.\n99\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019yinPhBqtj4zz7WeVeNdaj","session_id":"0e9f13f6-4032-41a4-8d9f-b9e18c221609","uuid":"9ebd2eed-faa8-4e77-b0a6-cda446f36fd5","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:39:32.868Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore Aurora revamp + strategy"}
