{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KgZX6uwVWZEbXoUXhKprxQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Awareness Revamp — Description\n2\t\n3\t**North Star (LOCKED 2026-06-11, John's verbatim intent):** Aurora exists to make John aware of all\n4\tcurrent advances in agentic AI — agentic systems, theories, approaches, advances in harnesses, the\n5\tmodels that feed them, the benchmarks, and new skills/templates/tools — serving THREE co-equal jobs:\n6\t(1) educate John, (2) guide his generation of new agents, (3) feed the agentic systems + Claude +\n7\tGemini via the Helping Hand retrieval skill. **Drift guard:** every surface or collection change must\n8\tserve awareness + adoption-decision + agent-feeding; a prettier ops console or richer taxonomy that\n9\tdoes not make John *more aware and better-decided* is bloat.\n10\t\n11\tThis phase evolves the *felt-value / awareness half* of the already-locked revamp. The dashboard\n12\tshipped and looks good, but using it exposed that Aurora optimizes for the wrong thing at the surface\n13\tand is mis-aimed at collection. Provenance: researchPrime report `docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/\n14\tRESEARCH.md` (adversarially validated — §B VALIDATED CORRECTIONS are binding) + handoff\n15\t`docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/HANDOFF.md`; Crucible Stage 0 framing + Stage 1 Master Plan (1\n16\tShark-Tank round, 3 BLOCKERs resolved, user-approved 2026-06-12) in this folder.\n17\t\n18\t## Five locked success criteria (each wave serves ≥1)\n19\t- **NS1 — Awareness:** per category (skills/tools/templates/agents/models) John can see \"current\n20\t  best-in-class + what newly moved + why it matters\" without leaving his morning report.\n21\t- **NS2 — Model+benchmark intelligence:** the 352 already-collected priced models are surfaced\n22\t  (junk-filtered) and a thin slice of benchmarks is collected + joined — answering \"which model for\n23\t  X, at what price/perf\" as a decision.\n24\t- **NS3 — Adoption decision:** candidate skills/tools/agents reach John as a fast, trustworthy\n25\t  *should-I-adopt?* call (summary/risks/advantages/why/effort); decisions are logged and become the\n26\t  label source for ranker validation (Helping-Hand auto-adoption is a FUTURE gate, not this phase).\n27\t- **NS4 — Right collection:** the nightly spend buys frontier-relevant agentic-AI items without\n28\t  losing recall on the obscure small-author find.\n29\t- **NS5 — Honest value:** a plain-English, no-vanity answer to \"is this working and worth its\n30\t  dollar,\" sample sizes shown, rates suppressed when ground truth is too thin.\n31\t\n32\t## Hard constraints (cross-cutting — apply to EVERY wave)\n33\t- **CC1 Publisher disposition.** Every new/changed table declares {scrub / publish-clean /\n34\t  publish-with-license-filter} and is **tested in `publisher --dry-run`** before the wave is done.\n35\t  The snapshot must drop any cell whose `license` is null/unknown or whose source is\n36\t  redistribution-restricted (OpenRouter ToS; Artificial-Analysis-derived scores). Default-publish of\n37\t  a new table is a defect. (publisher.py scrub block ~lines 210-251, BEFORE the final VACUUM.)\n38\t- **CC2 Live-pipeline safety.** Any collection/ingestion change lands behind a **shadow/dry-run**\n39\t  (write to `*_shadow`/fixture KB, no production writes, cost-capped, OFF the 01:07–06:47 cron),\n40\t  promoted only after a reviewed shadow diff. Reuse `roles/shadow_diff.py` + the `validations_shadow`\n41\t  pattern + `bin/run_security_shadow.py` as the template.\n42\t- **CC3 Honest-n.** No metric/ranking RATE is shown below **n<30**; show raw counts + window +\n43\t  sample size; name the open-loop state. Current adoption ground truth = n=7 decisions.\n44\t- **CC4** KB is **read-only except** the new `decisions`/`feedback` + the benchmark/model satellite\n45\t  tables. **Never** read `.env`. **Never** run `bin/migrate_to_kind_paper.py`'s delete step (it would\n46\t  delete legitimate local skills).\n47\t- **CC5 Provenance at write time.** Benchmark/model-derived cells carry NOT-NULL `source` + a\n48\t  license/`license_class` + `observed_at`/`scored_at` + contamination/`self_reported` flags; a null\n49\t  license is a write-time reject.\n50\t- **CC6 Report-first delivery.** Each wave's user-facing value ships as morning-report / weekly-email\n51\t  content first; dashboard surfaces are the optional drill-down, never the sole home of a deliverable.\n52\t- **CC7 Reuse, don't rebuild.** Evolve the existing `dashboard/` package + `kb/aurora.db` schema\n53\t  (additive migrations only; latest is `0025_interest_score.sql` → new migrations start at 0026).\n54\t\n55\t## Operational constraints (carried from CLAUDE.md / quality phase)\n56\t- The working tree **IS production**; scheduled tasks execute `C:\\dev\\aurora` directly (sweeps\n57\t  01:07–05:03, briefing 06:47). **Every wave ends with a clean committed tree.**\n58\t- Schema changes are idempotent migrations; scheduled tasks must not crash on a pre-migration DB\n59\t  (graceful fallback on missing tables/columns/env).\n60\t- Any wave touching `helping-hand-plugin/mcp-servers/aurora-kb/server.py` ends with plugin rebuild\n61\t  (`bin/build-plugin.py`) + reinstall (MANUAL — John installs in Cowork) + live smoke. (This phase\n62\t  is scoped to AVOID server.py where possible; W5 records via a dashboard endpoint, not the MCP.)\n63\t- **test-command:** `python -m pytest`. The existing test baseline stays green; no test weakening;\n64\t  the count may only rise.\n65\t\n66\t## Notable ground-truth refinements found at Stage 2 (verify by rule, counts drift nightly)\n67\t- `morning_briefing.py::_models_block()` ALREADY reads the `models` + `model_benchmarks` tables — so\n68\t  Wave 1's *briefing* surface is partly built; the gap is the dashboard surface + junk-filter +\n69\t  ensuring the `models` satellite table is populated.\n70\t- `roles/benchmark_scraper.py` ALREADY exists and targets **Artificial Analysis** — which RESEARCH\n71\t  §B flags as redistribution-restricted (free tier headline-only; redistribution needs a commercial\n72\t  contract). This is a latent CC1 leak: Wave 3 prefers **Epoch AI CC-BY** for the *published*\n73\t  library and MUST scrub AA-derived scores from the snapshot.\n74\t- `model_benchmarks` is empty not because nothing is built but because the scraper isn't wired/keyed.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019yinPhBqtj4zz7WeVeNdaj","session_id":"0e9f13f6-4032-41a4-8d9f-b9e18c221609","uuid":"ad604cde-54d9-4460-aac2-0cb1ecba8038","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:39:35.134Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore Aurora revamp + strategy"}
