{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AQ2WpJHc3ZHn22fwzZc91c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Awareness Revamp — Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\n2\t\n3\ttest-command: python -m pytest\n4\t\n5\t**North Star:** Make John aware of all current advances in agentic AI (systems/theories/harnesses/\n6\tmodels/benchmarks/skills/tools/templates) for 3 co-equal jobs — educate, guide agent-building, feed\n7\tHelping Hand — evolving the existing pipeline. Cross-cutting hard rules CC1–CC7 in `DESCRIPTION.md`\n8\tbind EVERY wave (publisher no-leak + dry-run; shadow before touching the live collector; no rate\n9\tbelow n<30; read-only KB except the new tables; write-time provenance; report-first delivery; reuse\n10\tnot rebuild). The working tree is production (sweeps 01:07–05:03, briefing 06:47): every wave ends\n11\twith a clean committed tree. Waves run in series.\n12\t\n13\t> Master plan + provenance: `STAGE1-MASTER-PLAN.md` (+ `STAGE0-FRAMING.md`); research base:\n14\t> `docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/RESEARCH.md` §B (binding). Code seams cited below are 2026-06-12\n15\t> snapshots (latest migration `0025_interest_score.sql`); line numbers drift — every wave resolves\n16\t> its real seam by SYMBOL (function/table name), never by the cited line alone.\n17\t\n18\t## Wave 1 — Surface the models we already own (the felt vertical)\n19\t\n20\t**Intent:** Make the 352 already-collected, fully-priced model rows visible — the highest\n21\tvalue-per-effort move (cost already paid, currently invisible). Report-first (CC6): a \"Models\"\n22\tsection in the morning report + weekly email, with the full sortable table + price/performance\n23\tfrontier on the dashboard as drill-down. No new external data (benchmarks come in Wave 3). Seed the\n24\tlabel-capture hook so adoption labels start accruing toward CC3's n≥30 immediately.\n25\t\n26\t**Deliverables:** A semantic + sentinel **junk-filter** for the `models`/artifacts join — exclude\n27\tprice sentinels (`price_in_usd_per_mtok <= 0 OR = -1000000`, `$0` rows) AND stale/deprecated/preview\n28\trows (`is_preview=1`, `deprecation_date < today`, stale `last_metadata_verified_at`) — expressed as a\n29\tsingle reusable SQL predicate constant (e.g. `dashboard/data/models.py::USABLE_MODEL_PREDICATE`) used\n30\tby every model surface; report the post-filter per-category counts. **Ensure the `models` satellite\n31\ttable is populated:** verify whether the models-sweep populates `models.*` for each `kind='model'`\n32\tartifact; if a gap exists, add `roles/librarian.py::_upsert_model_satellite(conn, artifact_id,\n33\tcandidate)` (parallel to the existing tool-install-note upsert) called from the models leg — INSERT\n34\tOR REPLACE on `artifact_id`, NOT-NULL `provider`/`family`/`license_class` (CC5). **NOTE (Stage-2\n35\tverified):** `roles/librarian.py` (~line 907) ALREADY upserts the `models` satellite idempotently with\n36\tNOT-NULL provider/family — so this deliverable is **\"verify populated, likely no-op,\"** not \"build a\n37\tnew function\"; only add `_upsert_model_satellite` if a real gap (e.g. missing `license_class`) is\n38\tfound by inspection. **Dashboard surface:**\n39\t`dashboard/data/catalog.py::models_summary()` + a `/api/catalog/models` route in\n40\t`dashboard/web/blueprint.py` returning the junk-filtered rows; a **sortable/filterable master table**\n41\t(provider/family/version, price in/out, context, max-out, modalities, reasoning_mode, tool_use,\n42\tlicense_class, cutoff, released_at) and a **price-performance frontier** as a static server-rendered\n43\tSVG (price-only axis until Wave 3) — reuse/refresh the existing `library/_model_grid.html` generator\n44\trather than adding a JS dependency (CC7). **Report surface:** extend the existing\n45\t`morning_briefing.py::_models_block()` and fold a `\"models\"` key\n46\t(`{total, new_by_provider, deprecating, license_distribution}`) into the **`bridge_data` dict in\n47\t`morning_briefing.py` (~line 1485) that writes `reports/morning/latest_summary.json`** — NOT\n48\t`exec_summary.py::write_summary()` (Stage-2 verified: that function writes per-sweep cost JSON, not\n49\t`latest_summary.json` — do not edit it). Then `briefing_delivery.build_session_note()` renders a scannable \"Models —\n50\t{total} tracked\" headline + new-by-provider + deprecating list + the weekly-email model-delta block.\n51\t**Label-capture seed:** add a non-authoritative 👍/👎 affordance on report/dashboard top-find items\n52\tthat POSTs to the Wave-5 decisions endpoint (stub the endpoint as a no-op-safe insert in W1 if W5\n53\tnot yet landed — guarded so a missing `decisions` table cannot crash the page). Additive tests:\n54\t`tests/test_models_surface.py` (predicate filters sentinels + preview/deprecated; summary counts;\n55\tsatellite upsert idempotent; briefing models block renders).\n56\t\n57\t**Depends on:** —\n58\t\n59\t**done-when:** Verifiable ON DEMAND — run `morning_briefing.py` + open the dashboard models surface\n60\tagainst the live KB: the models table renders only junk-filtered rows (zero `-1000000`/`$0`/preview\n61\trows), with per-category post-filter counts shown; the report's session_note carries a \"Models\"\n62\theadline with new-by-provider + deprecating; the price/perf frontier SVG renders from price data\n63\talone; the label-capture control is present and cannot crash on a missing decisions table; one clean\n64\tcommit; `python -m pytest` green with additive-only changes.\n65\t\n66\t- **Given** the live `models` table including `-1000000` and `$0` rows, **when** any model surface queries, **then** those rows are excluded by `USABLE_MODEL_PREDICATE` and the post-filter per-category count is reported. [SUBTLE — the sentinel-as-cheapest-model trap]\n67\t- **Given** a `kind='model'` artifact with no `models.*` satellite row, **when** the models leg runs, **then** `_upsert_model_satellite` populates it with NOT-NULL provider/family/license_class (idempotent on re-run).\n68\t- **Given** the briefing runs, **then** `latest_summary.json` carries a `models` key and the session_note renders a named Models headline (no raw IDs, no JSON shown to John).\n69\t- **Given** the `decisions` table does not yet exist, **when** the page renders the 👍/👎 control, **then** the page does not error (graceful-degrade).\n70\t\n71\t## Wave 2 — Re-aim the collector, behind a shadow (the existential fix)\n72\t\n73\t**Intent:** The starved collector (last night 8 papers, 0 skills/tools/agents) is the existential\n74\tNorth-Star failure. Add high-signal agentic sources + a frontier-relevance ranker that preserves\n75\trecall on the obscure find — built and proven ENTIRELY in shadow (CC2) before any production write or\n76\tcron promotion.\n77\t\n78\t**Deliverables:** New high-signal sources added to the seed map / scout config: **HF Daily Papers**\n79\t(`huggingface.co/api/daily_papers`, keyless — curated arxiv subset), **GitHub** new-repos by\n80\t**star-velocity** (Search API `topic:ai-agents/llm-agent/agent-framework` + `created:` recent),\n81\t**provider release feeds** (OpenAI/Anthropic/HF RSS), **trusted-aggregator** mentions (Smol AINews /\n82\tLatent Space) as a signal — wired through `roles/scout.py`'s existing source kinds (rss/json_api/\n83\ttopic_crawl), NOT new bespoke fetchers where a kind already fits. **Keep a narrow raw-arxiv recall\n84\tsafety net** (specific cs.AI/cs.MA + keyword) — arxiv is demoted, NOT cut to zero. **Frontier ranker**\n85\t`roles/frontier_ranker.py::frontier_score(artifact, signals) -> float` over cheap metadata\n86\t(provider_authority, trusted_aggregator_mention, stars_velocity, recency, benchmark_presence,\n87\tcode_linkage) with an explicit **authority-bypass lane**: strong `code_linkage + benchmark_presence +\n88\trecency` bypasses the provider-authority requirement so a non-famous high-signal repo still surfaces.\n89\t**Weights ship hand-set + flagged `validated=false`** (CC3 — no n≥30 labels yet); a `frontier_score`\n90\tcolumn is added (migration `0026_frontier_score.sql` — a SINGLE migration file carrying ALL of this\n91\twave's schema: the `frontier_score` column AND the `ranking_diffs` table below; do not create\n92\tcolliding `0026_*` files). **Shadow harness** `bin/run_ranker_shadow.py`\n93\t+ the `ranking_diffs` table (same migration `0026`): opens the KB read-only, runs the new ranker, compares\n94\tits top-N against the legacy `interest_score` order, writes a `reports/ranker_shadow/<date>.jsonl`\n95\tdiff; a promotion gate (reuse `roles/shadow_diff.py::promotion_gate` shape) requires the shadow\n96\tranking to NEVER demote an artifact a real user `loaded`. The new sources also run in shadow first\n97\t(a `--retarget-shadow` orchestrator flag writing to `*_shadow`/a fixture KB, cost-capped via a\n98\t`\"ranker_shadow\"` budget cell, OFF cron). **Nothing is promoted to the live cron in this wave** —\n99\tpromotion is a documented manual step after John reviews the shadow diff. Additive tests:\n100\t`tests/test_frontier_ranker.py` (authority-bypass surfaces a high-signal no-name repo; weights flagged\n101\tunvalidated; shadow gate blocks a loaded-artifact demotion; recall net keeps arxiv non-empty).\n102\t\n103\t**Depends on:** Wave 1\n104\t\n105\t**done-when:** The new sources + ranker run in **shadow only** (no production KB writes, off cron,\n106\tcost-capped) and emit a reviewable `reports/ranker_shadow/<date>.jsonl`; the authority-bypass lane is\n107\tfixture-proven to surface a non-famous high-signal item; weights are persisted `validated=false`; the\n108\traw-arxiv recall net is retained (fixture-proven non-empty); the promotion-to-cron step is documented\n109\tbut NOT taken; clean committed tree; `python -m pytest` green.\n110\t\n111\t- **Given** a brand-new repo from a non-famous author with linked runnable code + a benchmark result, **when** `frontier_score` runs, **then** the authority-bypass lane scores it above the surfacing gate (it is NOT filtered out by low provider-authority). [SUBTLE — the popularity-echo-chamber trap, RESEARCH §B-1]\n112\t- **Given** the new collector runs, **when** invoked without `--retarget-shadow`/promotion, **then** it makes ZERO writes to the production KB and is not on the nightly cron.\n113\t- **Given** a shadow ranking that would demote an artifact a real user `loaded`, **then** the promotion gate fails (blocks promotion).\n114\t- **Given** the retarget is active, **then** a narrow raw-arxiv query remains in the source set (recall net non-empty, fixture-proven).\n115\t\n116\t## Wave 3 — Benchmark thin-slice + decision-grade model view\n117\t\n118\t**Intent:** Turn the model price-sheet into a decision tool by collecting a thin, license-clean\n119\tbenchmark slice and joining it — unlocking \"best-for-X\" picks. Enforce the CC1 no-leak rule:\n120\tEpoch CC-BY is redistributable; Artificial-Analysis-derived and OpenRouter-derived data are NOT.\n121\t\n122\t**Deliverables:** **Schema first (BLOCKER fix, Stage-2 verified):** the live `model_benchmarks` table\n123\t(schema.sql ~291-302) has `source_url`/`scored_at`/`observed_at`/`contamination_flag` but **NO\n124\t`source` and NO `license` column** — and `benchmark_scraper.py` inserts without them. Add migration\n125\t`0027_benchmark_provenance.sql`: `ALTER TABLE model_benchmarks ADD COLUMN source TEXT` + `ADD COLUMN\n126\tlicense TEXT` (idempotent guard), and back-fill the existing `benchmark_scraper.py` INSERT to set them\n127\t(AA rows → `source='artificial-analysis'`, license per source). Without this migration the CC1 scrub\n128\t(`WHERE license IS NULL OR source IN (...)`) and the CC5 null-license write-reject have no columns to\n129\tact on and fail with \"no such column.\" Then add an **Epoch AI Benchmarking Hub** ingester (CSV ZIP\n130\tprimary, `pip install epochai` fallback) populating `model_benchmarks` (GPQA Diamond / SWE-bench Verified / FrontierMath /\n131\tMATH-L5 / AIME) with CC5 provenance per cell: NOT-NULL `source`, `license` (`CC-BY-4.0`; Aider/\n132\tTerminal-Bench rows `Apache-2.0`), `scored_at`/`observed_at`, `contamination_flag`. Match Epoch rows\n133\tto Aurora model artifacts by normalized key. **OpenRouter `/models`** used only as **transient\n134\tenrichment** for specs/pricing freshness (store derived facts, attribute, tolerate 401) — its derived\n135\tcells tagged `source='openrouter'` so CC1 can scrub them. The **existing `benchmark_scraper.py` (AA)**\n136\tstays usable for LOCAL viewing only if a key is present, but every AA-derived `model_benchmarks` row\n137\tis tagged `source='artificial-analysis'` and is **scrubbed from the publisher snapshot**. **Publisher\n138\tno-leak (CC1):** add a scrub statement in `publisher.py::build_snapshot()` BEFORE the final VACUUM —\n139\t`DELETE FROM model_benchmarks WHERE license IS NULL OR license NOT IN ('CC-BY-4.0','Apache-2.0') OR\n140\tsource IN ('artificial-analysis','openrouter')` — with the excluded set as an auditable constant; a\n141\tregression test in `tests/test_snapshot_scrub.py` asserts no AA/OpenRouter/null-license benchmark\n142\tcell survives the snapshot (env `AURORA_SECURITY_MODE` unset). **Sparse-aware composite:** compute a\n143\ttransparent composite ONLY over present component scores and **surface coverage/missing explicitly**\n144\t(never a black-box single index over missing cells); store as a derived view, not a hidden number.\n145\t**Best-for-X cards** (best coding / agentic / cheap-good / long-context / open-weights) on the Wave-1\n146\tmodel surface + a report line, each justified by the component score + provenance + an `as_of`\n147\tstaleness badge. Additive tests: `tests/test_benchmark_ingest.py` (Epoch rows carry license; null\n148\tlicense rejected at write — CC5) + the scrub regression above.\n149\t\n150\t**Depends on:** Wave 2\n151\t\n152\t**done-when:** `model_benchmarks` carries Epoch CC-BY rows with NOT-NULL source+license+scored_at; a\n153\twrite with null license is rejected; the publisher `--dry-run` snapshot contains ZERO AA-derived,\n154\tOpenRouter-derived, or null-license benchmark cells (regression-tested); best-for-X cards render with\n155\tprovenance + staleness badge and the composite shows its coverage; clean committed tree; `python -m\n156\tpytest` green.\n157\t\n158\t- **Given** an Epoch benchmark row, **when** ingested, **then** it carries `source='epoch'`, `license='CC-BY-4.0'`, `scored_at`; **given** a row with null license, **then** the write is rejected (CC5). [SUBTLE — the license-mislabel-becomes-leak trap]\n159\t- **Given** an AA-derived or OpenRouter-derived benchmark cell, **when** the publisher snapshot builds (`AURORA_SECURITY_MODE` unset), **then** the cell is absent from the snapshot (CC1 regression). [SUBTLE — the whole-DB-VACUUM-auto-publishes-new-tables trap]\n160\t- **Given** a model with only 2 of 5 component scores, **when** the composite renders, **then** it shows coverage (2/5) and never presents a single authoritative index over the 3 missing cells.\n161\t- **Given** the best-for-X cards, **then** each cites its justifying score + source + an `as_of` staleness badge.\n162\t\n163\t## Wave 4 — Awareness \"what moved\" + plain-English value/health\n164\t\n165\t**Intent:** Now that collection is fixed (W2) and benchmarks exist (W3), give John per-category \"what\n166\tmoved + why it matters\" and replace the unreadable health page's ROLE with a plain-English value +\n167\thealth summary — in the report (CC6), dashboard as drill-down. All metrics CC3 n-gated.\n168\t\n169\t**Deliverables:** **Per-category momentum:** promote the existing per-sweep deltas into a\n170\t\"what moved + why it matters\" report section across skills/tools/templates/agents/models, each item\n171\twith an opinionated one-line why, a hard top-N cap, and fade-after-N-nights; computed from sweep\n172\tdeltas (extend `walk_pipeline`/`walk_models_pipeline` to emit `new_today`/`delta` per kind into\n173\t`runs` + `latest_summary.json`). **Plain-English value+health:** a RAG (red/amber/green) + 4-question\n174\tsummary — *Is it working? / Is it worth it? / What's wrong? / What to think about?* — value-first,\n175\tzero JSON, in the report + weekly email; the dashboard keeps a human-readable `/api/health/summary`\n176\tpanel (concise `{ok, alerts, signals}`) with the existing detail endpoint as drill-down. **Metric set\n177\t(all CC3 n-gated, raw counts below n<30, window + sample_size shown):** useful-find rate (OMTM),\n178\tcost-per-useful-find, precision, frontier-coverage, decisions-influenced, spend-vs-budget. Reuse the\n179\tquality-phase precedent (`window`/`sample_size` fields, all-time fallback). Additive tests:\n180\t`tests/test_awareness_health.py` (n<30 suppresses the rate and shows raw count + window; momentum\n181\trespects top-N + fade; 4-question summary renders without JSON).\n182\t\n183\t**Depends on:** Wave 3\n184\t\n185\t**done-when:** The report carries a per-category \"what moved + why it matters\" section (top-N capped,\n186\tfade applied) and a plain-English RAG + 4-question value/health summary; every metric shows window +\n187\tsample_size and suppresses its rate below n<30 (showing raw counts); the dashboard health summary is\n188\thuman-readable; clean committed tree; `python -m pytest` green.\n189\t\n190\t- **Given** an adoption metric with n=7 (<30), **when** rendered, **then** the RATE is suppressed and a raw count + window + sample_size is shown instead. [SUBTLE — the 24%-over-n=7 vanity trap, RESEARCH §B-3]\n191\t- **Given** a category with 40 new items, **when** the momentum section renders, **then** it shows only the top-N with one-line whys and fades items older than N nights.\n192\t- **Given** the health summary renders, **then** it answers the 4 questions in plain English with zero JSON shown to John.\n193\t\n194\t## Wave 5 — Minimal, honest adoption (decisions + labels)\n195\t\n196\t**Intent:** Deliberately small (n=7 ground truth forbids automation). Render decision content in the\n197\treport, log accept/decline/snooze to a `decisions` table that DOUBLES as the label source for W2's\n198\tdeferred ranker validation. NO Helping-Hand auto-adoption — that is an explicit FUTURE gate at n≥30.\n199\t\n200\t**Deliverables:** Migration `0028_decisions.sql` (after W2's `0026`, W3's `0027`): `decisions(id, artifact_id FK,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019yinPhBqtj4zz7WeVeNdaj","session_id":"0e9f13f6-4032-41a4-8d9f-b9e18c221609","uuid":"56b05f59-205d-48a4-9eaf-f40d97460a12","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:39:35.383Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore Aurora revamp + strategy"}
