{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bk3Vs2LXH1L11mWzpctFcS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Awareness Revamp — researchPrime Report\n2\t\n3\t**Run:** 2026-06-11. **Mode:** ENGINE (node v26.1.0; import spike `go:true`, 28 trio symbols). **Sub-agent axis:** parallel-swarm. **ISOLATION:** real (fresh-context sub-agents). **Stakes tier:** MEDIUM (impact medium-high; reversibility high; blast-radius contained). **Adversarial pass:** RAN — 2 heterogeneous reviewers (≥2-agree) + context-free judge/synthesizer + 1 required blunt critic; 1 governed round, converged (consistent finding set, no new AXIS finding pending).\n4\t\n5\t**This report supersedes the raw execution briefs where the validation pass corrected them.** Read §B (validated corrections) as binding on the plan — several headline recommendations from the survey were downgraded or fenced by the adversarial round.\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n10\t\n11\tAurora already paid to collect the most valuable thing it has — **352 fully-priced model rows — and surfaces none of it.** It collects **zero benchmarks** though John explicitly wants \"the benches.\" Its discovery spend goes mostly to arxiv-paper harvesting, not the harnesses/models/skills the North Star names. The blunt verdict from the critic pass: **not yet worth it / marginal, and drifting toward \"dies looking healthy\"** — a polished, green-status, self-healing machine feeding a database nobody opens. The dollar isn't the problem; **attention asymmetry** is.\n12\t\n13\tThe research found strong, used-in-the-wild patterns for every surface John asked for. But the adversarial pass killed or fenced the most seductive ones:\n14\t\n15\t- **Highest value-per-effort, do first:** surface the 352-model table + an **intelligence-vs-cost (price/performance) frontier** view with **best-for-X** cards. The data exists; the cost is already paid. *This is the one recommendation whose value doesn't depend on usage history — protect it.*\n16\t- **Collect benchmarks (thin slice):** OpenRouter `/models` (pricing/specs, keyless) + **Epoch AI CC-BY** (GPQA/SWE-bench/FrontierMath, mirror-legal) are the tonight-grade pair. Compute your *own* composite from raw component scores; never ingest a black-box index; stamp `source`+`as_of`+`self_reported` on every cell.\n17\t- **Adoption surface:** keep the decision-card *content* spec, but the keyboard-triage queue is **over-engineered for ~2 decisions/week** — deliver it through the **morning report** (where John already lives), not a surface he must visit. Any auto-recommendation is a **non-authoritative suggestion**, never a consensus verdict.\n18\t- **Knowledge map:** the UMAP+HDBSCAN+deck.gl \"data map\" is **NOT dependency-light/offline** on a Windows nightly (llvmlite/numba native-build fragility) and is the **least decision-useful** build. If built: use **precomputed PCA/TruncatedSVD (pure sklearn/numpy) + plain canvas**, isolate it so its failure can't break ingestion, and treat it as secondary.\n19\t- **Collection retargeting — biggest landmine:** the survey's instinct (cut arxiv → HF Daily Papers; gate on a provider-authority-weighted `frontier_score`) **narrows discovery toward popularity at both ends** and structurally filters out the obscure small-author find John values most. **Keep a narrow raw-arxiv recall safety net; add an authority-bypass lane to the score; validate weights against John's real liked/rejected labels.**\n20\t- **Honest value:** RAG + 4-question plain-English summary, headline metric **cost per *useful* find** — but **suppress all rates below an n-floor (n<30 → show raw counts)**; current adoption ground truth is **n=7 decisions** (6 loaded, 1 dismissed across 3 weeks). Name the bootstrap/open-loop problem explicitly.\n21\t\n22\t**The cheapest thing that prevents quiet failure:** push **one weekly email** — model-board delta (new/cheaper models), benchmark movement, the single best non-paper find, and one honest line \"Aurora fed your sessions N times.\" If that email isn't worth 30 seconds, that *is* the verdict — and it's cheaper to learn from one cron job than six more months of $1 nights.\n23\t\n24\t---\n25\t\n26\t## A. SURVEY FINDINGS (per §5 question)\n27\t\n28\t### Q1 — Awareness surfaces for fast-moving fields\n29\tExemplars (OBSERVED): ThoughtWorks Technology Radar, State of AI Report (Air Street), Artificial Analysis, LMArena, the *retired* HF Open LLM Leaderboard, Rundown/TLDR/Neuron newsletters.\n30\t\n31\tPatterns that make a surface **used vs ignored**:\n32\t1. **Readiness verdict, coarse buckets** — adopt/trial/assess/hold *recommended action*, not a score. (DECISION) [CORROBORATED]\n33\t2. **Opinionated POV over neutral dump** — neutral exhaustive lists get ignored. (both) [CORROBORATED]\n34\t3. **\"Why it matters\" one-liner per item** — the education→decision bridge; Rundown's ~50% open rate. (both) [CORROBORATED]\n35\t4. **Movement/momentum** — \"what changed since last time\"; items fade after N of no movement. (both) [OBSERVED]\n36\t5. **Multi-axis comparison, not single rank.** (DECISION) [CORROBORATED]\n37\t6. **Fixed cadence + hard volume cap.** (EDUCATION) [CORROBORATED]\n38\t7. **Accountability loop** — grade last period's calls (State of AI grades its predictions). [CORROBORATED]\n39\t\n40\tAnti-patterns: single leaderboard rank as ground truth (the HF Open LLM Leaderboard **died** of contamination + hill-climbing [CORROBORATED]); neutral dump with no verdict; volume over signal; stale artifact with no \"what's new\"; gameable single metric.\n41\t\n42\t### Q2 — Best-in-class model intelligence\n43\tPresentation patterns that work (OBSERVED across Artificial Analysis / OpenRouter / LMArena / llm-stats / Epoch): **intelligence-vs-cost quadrant / Pareto frontier scatter** (the single most decision-useful artifact); speed-vs-quality; **\"best for X\" curated cards**; tiering with confidence intervals (not bare ranks); sortable master table; open-vs-proprietary lens.\n44\t\n45\tMachine-collectable source shortlist (ranked, with the validation carve-outs applied — see §B):\n46\t| # | Source | Access | Yields | License caveat |\n47\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n48\t| 1 | **OpenRouter `/api/v1/models`** | keyless JSON (verified HTTP 200) | pricing, context, modalities, reasoning, cutoff, `benchmarks` field | **ToS forbids scraping/redistribution → transient enrichment only, store derived facts, attribute** |\n49\t| 2 | **Epoch AI Benchmarking Hub** | CSV ZIP + `pip install epochai` | GPQA Diamond, SWE-bench Verified, FrontierMath, MATH-L5, AIME | **CC-BY 4.0 (mirror-legal)** — but MMLU-Pro absent; Aider/Terminal-Bench rows are Apache-2.0 (per-row license) |\n50\t| 3 | **SWE-bench `leaderboards.json`** | raw GitHub file | % resolved (Verified/Lite/MM) | permissive; trust \"Verified\" split (self-reported) |\n51\t| 4 | **LiveCodeBench** | HF Space/datasets | contamination-controlled code | self-reported PRs |\n52\t| 5 | **LMArena** | **no official API** → Apache-2.0/MIT community daily mirrors | human-pref Elo + CI | gameable; cite \"Source: LMArena\"; store CI |\n53\t| — | **Artificial Analysis Data API** | REST, keyed | composite indices | **free tier = headline only, 100/day; redistribution needs commercial contract → reference, not feed** |\n54\t\n55\t### Q3 — Adoption-decision UX\n56\tDecision-card fields (ranked): `what_it_is` (1 line) · `fit_reason` (why it surfaced for *you* — the top differentiator) · `recommendation`+`confidence` · `advantages[3]` · `risks[]` (license/security/maintenance/malicious flags) · `provenance{author, source_url, age, adoption, scorecard}` · `effort` · `evidence_link` (collapsed). Interaction: pre-computed verdict the human *ratifies* (Renovate \"Merge Confidence\" beats Dependabot); ≤3 actions, single-key, **reversible + snooze**; cap & cluster nightly queue (Dependabot security PRs hit only ~13% adoption from noise). Persist decisions in SQLite. [OBSERVED/CORROBORATED — see §B for the \"deliver via report, not heavy queue\" correction.]\n57\t\n58\t### Q4 — Knowledge / relationship map\n59\tSurvey recommended a **clustered embedding projection** (UMAP→HDBSCAN→c-TF-IDF labels, DataMapPlot/deck.gl) over a force-directed graph (which hairballs and needs edges Aurora lacks). Relatedness = 2-D position; clusters = emergent classification. **The validation pass refuted \"dependency-light/offline\" and the build-priority — see §B.** Comparison: concept maps (manual, unscalable); force-directed (hairball); landscape/quadrant (needs pre-known axes); Sankey (no flows here); Voronoi treemap (= the rejected catalog map). Secondary affordance worth keeping: precomputed top-k k-NN egonet rendered only on click (never the global graph).\n60\t\n61\t### Q5 — Collection targeting\n62\tSource portfolio: **Tier-1 add** — HF Daily Papers API (keyless, ~20-30/day curated) + HF Hub models (likes7d), GitHub Search API (`topic:ai-agents`/`llm-agent`/`agent-framework`, `created:` recent, **sort by star-velocity**), provider release feeds (OpenAI/Anthropic/HF RSS + llm-stats/aireleasetracker), Smol AINews + Latent Space (trusted-aggregator *mention* = signal). **Tier-2** — per-repo GitHub Releases for a fixed harness watchlist (LangGraph, CrewAI, AutoGen/AG2, OpenAI Agents SDK, Claude Agent SDK, smolagents, Dify, Langflow, Flowise, MetaGPT); agent benchmark releases (SWE-bench Verified, GAIA, OSWorld, Tau²-Bench, WebArena, METR — treat *release/presence* as signal, scores are gameable); HN Algolia (Show HN) + Product Hunt Atom. **Cut/demote** raw arxiv bulk → resolver only. Ranking heuristic `frontier_score` (auth 35 / aggregator 25 / star-velocity 20 / recency 10 / bench 5 / code 5, gate ≥55). **The validation pass found this stacks a popularity bias — see §B; it is the single biggest risk in the set.**\n63\t\n64\t### Q6 — Honest value framing\n65\tVanity→actionable map: items collected→items opened/adopted; library size→**frontier coverage/recall**; sweeps GREEN→**cost per *useful* find**; tokens spent→**decisions influenced**; finds/night→**precision (signal/noise)**; self-heals→**misses prevented**. Tiny metric set (≤6): (1) useful-find rate [OMTM], (2) cost/useful-find, (3) precision, (4) frontier coverage/recall, (5) decisions/awareness influenced, (6) spend-vs-budget. Health summary = **RAG light + 4 plain questions**: *Is it working? / Is it worth it? / What's wrong? / What to think about?* — value-first, zero JSON. Guardrails (bands not targets): precision floor, recall floor, duplicate-rate ceiling, owner false-positive ceiling.\n66\t\n67\t---\n68\t\n69\t## B. VALIDATED CORRECTIONS (adversarial pass — BINDING on the plan)\n70\t\n71\tThese are the ≥2-agree / empirically-checked findings that override the raw survey. **The Crucible plan must encode these as constraints.**\n72\t\n73\t1. **[BLOCKER] Discovery is being narrowed toward popularity at both ends.** Cutting raw arxiv → HF Daily Papers filters input to ~2-3% trending (recall-lossy, hype-biased, Gemini-tagged), and `frontier_score` puts **80/100 points on provider-authority + aggregator-mention + stars** — a brand-new non-famous tool caps at ~20, far below the 55 gate. Stacked, the system *structurally cannot surface the obscure small-author find that justifies Aurora's existence* (the exact \"deep think skill\" class John liked). **Fix:** keep a narrow raw-arxiv recall safety net (specific cs.AI/cs.MA + keyword); add an **authority-bypass lane** (strong code_linkage + benchmark_presence + recency bypasses authority); down-weight provider_authority/stars; **validate weights against a labeled set of John's past liked-vs-rejected finds before trusting any cutoff.** [Reviewer A empirical: HF Daily ~20-30/day vs arxiv ~1000/day, HTTP-verified; Reviewer B concurs on hype-bias.]\n74\t\n75\t2. **[BLOCKER] Auto-computed readiness ring manufactures false consensus over near-zero ground truth.** ThoughtWorks rings work *because* humans argue each blip; auto-deriving adopt/trial/assess/hold from existing fields keeps the visual authority and strips the trust basis. With n=7 real decisions it can't be calibrated against anything. One confidently-wrong \"ADOPT\" and John discounts the ring permanently. **Fix:** demote to a **non-authoritative tag** (\"model suggests: trial\"), never a ring implying consensus. [Reviewer B; critic concurs.]\n76\t\n77\t3. **[MAJOR] Adoption metrics are currently vanity dressed as actionable.** Live `hh_events`: 106 events but only **7 carry a decision** (6 loaded, 1 dismissed) across 21 queries / 10 sessions / 3 weeks. \"Cost per useful find,\" precision, adoption rate all divide by ~7 → noise with a decimal point. **Fix:** every metric renders its `n` inline; **suppress the rate entirely below a floor (n<30) and show raw counts**; the plan must explicitly name that until usage exists, every learned/derived signal (taste, precision, ring) runs **open-loop**. [Reviewer B empirical pull; aligns with the locked discovery-quality plan's \"window labeled, sample size shown.\"]\n78\t\n79\t4. **[MAJOR] \"UMAP + DataMapPlot/deck.gl is dependency-light/offline\" is REFUTED on Windows nightly.** umap-learn/hdbscan pull scikit-learn; UMAP pulls numba→llvmlite (vendored LLVM, notorious Windows wheel/native-build failures; a Python minor bump can drop the wheel and hard-crash the 01:07 sweep). deck.gl is hundreds of KB. **Fix:** if a map is built, use **precomputed PCA/TruncatedSVD (pure sklearn/numpy) + plain `<canvas>`**; vendor any JS locally; **isolate the map build so its failure cannot take down ingestion.** Also it's the **least decision-useful** item (an unsupervised projection is the same *class* John rejected) — down-weight its build priority vs model-intelligence. [Reviewer A native-dep evidence; Reviewer B value.]\n80\t\n81\t5. **[MAJOR] OpenRouter is keyless but ToS forbids scraping/redistribution.** Verified HTTP 200 no-auth, but their Terms prohibit automated scraping/copying and reselling. A verbatim nightly mirror into the published `aurora-library` violates ToS even private. **Fix:** treat as **transient enrichment** — store *derived facts*, not verbatim catalog dumps; attribute; build for the endpoint flipping to 401; don't hammer (no published rate limit). [Reviewer A, ToS-checked.]\n82\t\n83\t6. **[MINOR] Epoch CC-BY confirmed with carve-outs:** MMLU-Pro is **not** in Epoch's set (don't assume that column); Aider Polyglot / Terminal-Bench rows are **Apache-2.0** → carry **per-source license metadata**, not one global attribution string. CSV ZIP is the durable feed; pip is the fallback. [Reviewer A, license-checked, CSV updated today.]\n84\t\n85\t7. **[STRATEGIC] The 80/20 is the morning report, not new surfaces.** John consumes via the report (which he called \"fine\"), not by visiting pages; the prior dashboard's value gap existed *because* output \"was only written to disk.\" Provider-feed/star-velocity collection (better inputs), provenance/freshness tags, model-board deltas, and the 4-question value summary all land **inside the report**. A daily keyboard-triage queue optimizes a turnstile that sees ~2 decisions/week. [Reviewer B + critic converge.]\n86\t\n87\t**Cut (reviewer consensus):** the **auto-computed readiness *ring*** (false consensus, highest trust-downside). Runner-up cut/down-weight: the UMAP map.\n88\t**Protect (reviewer consensus):** the **intelligence-vs-cost model view + best-for-X cards + pricing + benchmarks** — the one recommendation whose value doesn't depend on usage history; the data is objective and already collected.\n89\t\n90\t---\n91\t\n92\t## C. THE BLUNT CRITIQUE (required deliverable, no flattery)\n93\t\n94\t**Is Aurora worth running today? Not yet — marginal, and drifting the wrong way.** Stripped of framing, a night delivers 8-21 arxiv papers + ~20 rejections to a polished read-only dashboard; last night produced **zero** skills/tools/agents. The system built to track harnesses/models/benchmarks/skills spent its dollar on the one category John mentioned in passing and can get free from a dozen newsletters. Of the three co-equal jobs — educate / guide agent-building / feed retrieval — it weakly does a fraction of #1 (paper awareness, only if John opens the dashboard) and essentially not #2 or #3. **The polish is working against honesty: it looks finished, so value is assumed that isn't there.**\n95\t\n96\t**The 3-5 changes that would make it genuinely valuable (ranked):**\n97\t1. **Surface the models table this week.** 352 priced rows already exist; build one sortable/filterable board, drop junk rows. Highest value-per-effort in the project — the cost is already paid. *Felt:* the first time it answers \"cheapest model >200k context with tool use, released this quarter\" without a browser tab, it stops being a science project.\n98\t2. **Collect benchmarks, even a thin slice.** John named \"the benches\"; the table is empty. Two public leaderboards keyed to existing models turns the price sheet into a *decision tool*. *Felt:* Aurora becomes the place he checks before picking a model.\n99\t3. **Re-aim collection off arxiv toward harnesses/skills/tools.** 8 papers / 0 tools is mis-tuned. *Felt:* the briefing stops reading like a free arxiv digest and tells him things he didn't know.\n100\t4. **Close the taste loop with one-click rating in the briefing.** 30 finds is too thin to steer anything. *Felt:* the system getting *more his* over weeks.\n101\t5. **Make Helping Hand actually fire and prove it.** \"Surfaced, never loaded\" = theater. Lower the gate, instrument real loads, put \"Aurora fed your sessions N times\" in the briefing. *Felt:* job #3 goes from claim to number.\n102\t\n103\t**Most likely quiet failure:** it keeps running flawlessly, stays green and polished, and John stops opening it — failure by *irrelevance*, not breakage. Self-healing makes this *more* likely: nothing alarms, so nothing prompts a rethink. It dies looking healthy. **Cheapest prevention:** the weekly email above.\n104\t\n105\t---\n106\t\n107\t## D. AGENT-IMPLEMENTATION SUMMARY (for the Crucible planner / Foreman)\n108\t\n109\tConstraints to encode (from §B, binding):\n110\t- **Reuse, don't rebuild:** read-only dashboard package (`dashboard/`), `kb/aurora.db` schema; evolve.\n111\t- **Sequencing by value-per-effort:** (1) model-intelligence surface from the existing 352 rows + price/perf frontier + best-for-X; (2) benchmark ingestion (OpenRouter keyless + Epoch CC-BY; compute own composite; `source`+`as_of`+`self_reported` per cell); (3) collection retargeting *with recall safety net + authority-bypass + label-validated weights*; (4) adoption decision-cards delivered through the report; (5) value/health = RAG + 4-question, n-gated metrics; (6) knowledge map LAST, optional, PCA+canvas, isolated.\n112\t- **Hard rules:** OpenRouter = transient enrichment (no verbatim redistribution; attribute; tolerate 401). Per-row benchmark license metadata. No auto \"ring\" implying consensus — non-authoritative suggestion only. Suppress rates below n<30. Keep a narrow raw-arxiv recall net. UMAP/numba must NOT be on the ingestion critical path (isolate or avoid via PCA). Validate `frontier_score` weights against John's liked/rejected labels before trusting any gate. Junk-filter the models table (-1000000 sentinel, $0 rows).\n113\t- **The cross-cutting win:** push value into the morning report/weekly email, not surfaces John must visit.\n114\t\n115\t**Evidence honesty:** OpenRouter keyless, Epoch CC-BY+update-date, HF Daily volume, `hh_events` n=7, llvmlite/numba Windows failures, OpenRouter ToS = all OBSERVED/empirically-checked this run. Presentation patterns (radar rings, Pareto frontier, decision cards, RAG reporting, vanity-vs-actionable) = CORROBORATED. Intelligence-value framings (decision advantage, VOI) = CLAIMED single-source. No claim is BANDWAGON-ONLY. The vanity/actionable application to Aurora is reasoning over corroborated frameworks, not a measurement.\n116\t"}]},"paren