{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NJG8JzyLkkd3deo2KttsC1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Aurora orchestrator — entry point for nightly sweeps.\n2\t\n3\tUsage:\n4\t    python -m aurora.orchestrator --sweep skills              # live sweep\n5\t    python -m aurora.orchestrator --sweep skills --dry-run    # walk pipeline, no LLM calls\n6\t    python -m aurora.orchestrator --sweep skills --no-swarm   # skip runner+critics+reconciler (P2 mode)\n7\t\"\"\"\n8\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n9\timport argparse\n10\timport asyncio\n11\timport contextlib\n12\timport hashlib\n13\timport json\n14\timport logging\n15\timport os\n16\timport shutil\n17\timport sqlite3\n18\timport sys\n19\timport tempfile\n20\timport time\n21\tfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n22\tfrom pathlib import Path\n23\tfrom typing import Optional\n24\t\n25\timport yaml\n26\tfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\n27\t\n28\tfrom aurora.sweeps import SWEEP_CONFIGS, SweepConfig\n29\tfrom aurora.roles import scout, quarantine as quarantine_role, static_screener\n30\tfrom aurora.roles import sanitizer as sanitizer_role\n31\tfrom aurora.roles import embedder, librarian\n32\tfrom aurora.roles import runner as runner_role\n33\tfrom aurora.roles import critic_a, critic_b, critic_c, reconciler\n34\tfrom aurora.roles import batch_sweep\n35\tfrom aurora.roles import evidence, shadow_diff\n36\tfrom aurora.roles import model_card_parser, benchmark_scraper, literature_reviewer, pricing_collector\n37\t# Wave-C (2026-05-25): advisor replaces literature_reviewer's call site below.\n38\t# We keep the literature_reviewer import for a 1-week rollback window.\n39\tfrom aurora.roles import advisor as advisor_role\n40\tfrom aurora.llm import CostRecorder\n41\tfrom aurora.exec_summary import write_summary, mtd_per_vendor\n42\t\n43\tlog = logging.getLogger(\"aurora.orchestrator\")\n44\t\n45\tROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n46\tDB_PATH = ROOT / \"kb\" / \"aurora.db\"\n47\tLOCK_PATH = ROOT / \"lock\" / \"sweep.lock\"\n48\tLOG_DIR = ROOT / \"logs\"\n49\tLIBRARY_ROOT = ROOT / \"library\"\n50\tREPORTS_ROOT = ROOT / \"reports\"\n51\t\n52\tMONTHLY_CAPS = {\"anthropic\": 50.00, \"gemini\": 10.00}\n53\t\n54\t# Bucket J4 (v4.3, 2026-05-19 PM): per-sweep budget guardrail.\n55\t# Bucket O-12 (2026-05-23): per-role budget cells. The 15-20% overshoot pattern\n56\t# from J4 was critic_b-token-blowup-dominated; per-role cells isolate which\n57\t# throttle. The total still applies (sum of cells ≤ PER_SWEEP_BUDGET_USD).\n58\t# Cells are PROPORTIONAL — derived from observed nightly cost ratios. Adjust\n59\t# as the system grows; the guardrail prefers conservative (lower) caps.\n60\t_SWEEPS_PER_DAY = 3\n61\t_DAYS_PER_MONTH = 30\n62\tPER_SWEEP_BUDGET_USD = MONTHLY_CAPS[\"anthropic\"] / _DAYS_PER_MONTH / _SWEEPS_PER_DAY\n63\t\n64\t# Per-role cells. Sum is < PER_SWEEP_BUDGET_USD on purpose (headroom). Any cell\n65\t# crossing trips the same 'partial' status as the total cap.\n66\tPER_ROLE_BUDGET_USD = {\n67\t    \"scout\":       PER_SWEEP_BUDGET_USD * 0.05,\n68\t    \"sanitizer\":   PER_SWEEP_BUDGET_USD * 0.10,\n69\t    \"runner\":      PER_SWEEP_BUDGET_USD * 0.35,\n70\t    \"critic_a\":    PER_SWEEP_BUDGET_USD * 0.15,\n71\t    \"critic_b\":    PER_SWEEP_BUDGET_USD * 0.15,\n72\t    # Wave 1 (2026-06-02): critic_c's third-judge provider calls (DeepSeek/Groq)\n73\t    # now flow through CostRecorder. Small cell — critic_c runs on cheap/free-tier\n74\t    # cross-family providers, so its expected spend is the lowest of the judges.\n75\t    \"critic_c\":    PER_SWEEP_BUDGET_USD * 0.05,\n76\t    \"reconciler\":  PER_SWEEP_BUDGET_USD * 0.10,\n77\t    # Wave 2 / H2 (2026-06-06): defense-in-depth cap on the evidence-loop SHADOW\n78\t    # re-scoring spend. With the default-off live re-score\n79\t    # (AURORA_EVIDENCE_LIVE_RESCORE unset) the nightly path uses the precomputed\n80\t    # zero-cost score_fn, so this cell is normally 0. It only bites when the live\n81\t    # re-score IS enabled, bounding it via _role_budget_exceeded(\"evidence_shadow\").\n82\t    # Conservative: it re-runs the same panel the legacy verdict already pays for,\n83\t    # so size it like the panel's own cells (a/b/c+reconciler ~= 0.45 combined);\n84\t    # cap at the reconciler cell so it can never dwarf the live verdict spend.\n85\t    \"evidence_shadow\": PER_SWEEP_BUDGET_USD * 0.10,\n86\t    \"embedder\":    PER_SWEEP_BUDGET_USD * 0.05,\n87\t    \"literature_reviewer\": PER_SWEEP_BUDGET_USD * 0.03,\n88\t    \"pricing_collector\":   PER_SWEEP_BUDGET_USD * 0.05,\n89\t    # Awareness Revamp Wave 2 (2026-06-12): cap on the SHADOW-ONLY retarget\n90\t    # pass (new high-signal sources + frontier ranker, via --retarget-shadow).\n91\t    # Normally 0 — it only meters when --retarget-shadow is set, which is OFF\n92\t    # the nightly cron. Small cell: the shadow pass is cheap-metadata scoring,\n93\t    # not a full swarm.\n94\t    \"ranker_shadow\": PER_SWEEP_BUDGET_USD * 0.08,\n95\t}\n96\t\n97\t\n98\tdef _sweep_cost_so_far(conn: sqlite3.Connection, run_id: int) -> float:\n99\t    \"\"\"Sum of usd_estimate for this run across all cost_recorder writes so far.\n100\t    Cheap (single SUM over an indexed-by-run-id table) — fine to call after"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01UkhjqCpsBaWTEbkLkiiJeJ","session_id":"0e9f13f6-4032-41a4-8d9f-b9e18c221609","uuid":"05995ad4-af19-4be4-9b27-b0ba9c0e4f44","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:39:38.121Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore Aurora core architecture"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016kQxfGyTEMmW8fyo2AJDv5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Awareness Revamp — Execution Log\n2\t\n3\tThis log is written by Foreman as it executes the waves in `IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md`. It starts empty.\n4\t\n5\t**Handoff status (2026-06-12):** Crucible Stage 0 (North Star locked) + Stage 1 (Master Plan,\n6\tuser-approved, map deferred) + Stage 2 (this doc-trio) complete. Research base:\n7\t`docs/aurora-awareness-revamp/RESEARCH.md` (adversarially validated). Not yet started by Foreman.\n8\t\n9\t| Wave | Status | Commit | Notes |\n10\t|---|---|---|---|\n11\t| 1 — Surface models we own | ✅ GREEN | (this commit) | 321/352 usable surfaced; report+dashboard+SVG; +13 tests |\n12\t| 2 — Re-aim collector (shadow) | ✅ GREEN | (this commit) | frontier_ranker + authority-bypass; shadow-only, CC2 airtight; +19 tests |\n13\t| 3 — Benchmark slice + decision view | ✅ GREEN | (this commit) | Epoch CC-BY ingester + CC1 scrub (both directions verified); +12 tests |\n14\t| 4 — Awareness + value/health | ✅ GREEN | (this commit) | momentum + 4-question RAG; §B-3 n-gated (terminal not surfaced); +16 tests |\n15\t| 5 — Minimal adoption (decisions) | ✅ GREEN | (this commit) | decisions table + capture; CC1 scrub + §B-2 non-authoritative; +17 tests |\n16\t\n17\t**PROJECT COMPLETE — all 5 waves GREEN (2026-06-12).** Test baseline 1076 →\n18\t**1152 passed** (+76 additive; the lone failing `test_no_stale_running_runs_from_\n19\tyesterday` is a pre-existing, unrelated live-DB stale-`runs` artifact present\n20\tbefore W1, left untouched per CC4).\n21\t\n22\t### ✅ RESOLVED 2026-06-13 — the \"live-DB migration breakage\" was a FALSE ALARM\n23\tThe Wave-3 ⚠ escalation (apply_migrations \"fails on the live DB with no such\n24\ttable: helping_hand_log\") was a **measurement error, not a real bug.** Root\n25\tcause: `kb/aurora.db` runs in **WAL journal mode**, and I diagnosed it by\n26\t`cp kb/aurora.db /tmp/...` — which copies ONLY the main file, omitting the\n27\t`-wal`, producing an INCONSISTENT snapshot missing recently-committed objects\n28\t(`helping_hand_log`, fresh `schema_version` rows). `apply_migrations` then failed\n29\ton that broken copy. The real DB, read coherently (a `mode=ro` sqlite connection\n30\tor the `.backup()` API, both of which merge WAL+main), was always healthy.\n31\t**Verified 2026-06-13:** (1) the overnight nightly sweep applied `0026/0027/0028`\n32\tcleanly — live `schema_version` now holds 26, 27, 28; `artifacts.frontier_score`,\n33\t`model_benchmarks.source/license`, and the `decisions` table all exist in\n34\tproduction. (2) On a CONSISTENT copy (sqlite `.backup()`), `apply_migrations` is a\n35\tclean no-op (`[]` twice) with NO helping_hand_log error. (3) No version\n36\tcollisions — 26/27/28 are declared only by my three files; the migration version\n37\tnumbers are scrambled vs filename prefixes (e.g. `0001_hh_telemetry.sql` →\n38\tv32), and 1/2/29/30 are simply unused target numbers (benign). **Nothing to\n39\trepair. All W2–W5 schema is live.** Remaining activation is DATA, not schema:\n40\t`model_benchmarks` is empty until the Epoch ingester is run (then best-for-X\n41\tcards + composite light up); `decisions` accrue as the 👍/👎 control is used; the\n42\tfrontier ranker stays shadow-only by design until n≥30 labels.\n43\t\n44\t**Lesson (do not repeat):** never diagnose a WAL-mode SQLite DB by copying just\n45\tthe `.db` file. Use a `mode=ro` connection or `sqlite3 .backup()` for a coherent\n46\tsnapshot.\n47\t\n48\t---\n49\t\n50\t## Wave 5 — Minimal, honest adoption (decisions + labels) — GREEN (2026-06-12)\n51\t\n52\tEXECUTE → orchestrator-run gate → 2 reviewers (I = CC1/§B-2/anti-test-weakening;\n53\tJ = capture correctness + production-safety; **both GO**) → 1 bounded hardening\n54\tFIX → re-gate. **Gate: 1135 → 1152 passed** (+17 additive; same 1 pre-existing\n55\tunrelated `runs` failure). Deliberately small (n=7 forbids automation; NO\n56\tHelping-Hand auto-adoption — that's a FUTURE gate at n≥30).\n57\t\n58\t**Delivered:** migration `0028_decisions.sql` — `decisions(id, artifact_id FK,\n59\tdecision_type CHECK IN ('adopt','defer','reject','retire'), reason,\n60\texplicit_label, explicit_confidence, made_at, made_by_session_id, recorded_at)` +\n61\tindexes (idempotent; schema.sql mirrored). `/api/decisions/record` upgraded from\n62\tthe W1 graceful stub to a real insert (resolve slug→artifact_id, 👍→adopt /\n63\t👎→reject, validates decision_type in Python before insert so a bad type returns\n64\t200 `{ok:false}` not a 500; still 200 `{ok:false}` when the table is absent —\n65\tthe live state). `bin/record-decision.py` CLI for offline logging.\n66\t`_decisions_block` renders decision cards (what-it-is / fit / advantages / risks /\n67\tprovenance / effort) with a **non-authoritative \"model suggests: trial/assess\"**\n68\trecommendation — confidence caps at \"medium\" even at high interest_score; header\n69\t\"(suggestions — not verdicts)\"; NO authoritative ADOPT/consensus ring can render\n70\t(§B-2). Honest \"Decisions logged this week: N (need ≥30 to validate the ranker)\"\n71\tcounter (CC3): N raw, no rate below the floor; distinguishes present-empty\n72\t(\"0, need ≥30\") from table-absent (\"capture not yet provisioned\").\n73\t\n74\t**CC1 — decisions NEVER published (load-bearing):** `publisher.py` SCRUB adds\n75\t`DROP TABLE IF EXISTS decisions` before VACUUM (private adoption labels). Reviewer\n76\tI built a real snapshot with a seeded private-marker decision and confirmed the\n77\ttable AND the marker BYTES are absent from the post-VACUUM snapshot\n78\t(`secure_delete=ON`). Regression-locked in `test_snapshot_scrub.py` +\n79\t`test_decisions.py`.\n80\t\n81\t**Anti-test-weakening (Foreman §5) — cleared.** W5 added `decisions` to\n82\tschema.sql, so `build_kb` now creates it, which would have broken 4 W4-era\n83\t\"table-absent\" graceful-degrade tests. They were reconciled by ADDING\n84\t`DROP TABLE IF EXISTS decisions` to reproduce the live (migration-blocked)\n85\ttable-absent state — **no assertion removed/loosened** (orchestrator-diffed +\n86\tReviewer-I-verified line by line); total count rose 1135→1152, no skip/xfail.\n87\t\n88\t**FIX (review NITs, proportionate hardening for the unattended 06:47 job):**\n89\twrapped `_decisions_counter` in the same try/except guard as `_decisions_block`\n90\t(neither can crash the briefing; `None` is rendered-safe downstream) and pinned\n91\tthe present-but-empty counter path with a regression test.\n92\t\n93\t**No server.py / plugin change** (records via the dashboard endpoint, not the\n94\tMCP) — no plugin rebuild. KB writes scoped to the `decisions` table only (CC4).\n95\t\n96\t## Wave 4 — Awareness \"what moved\" + plain-English value/health — GREEN (2026-06-12)\n97\t\n98\tEXECUTE → orchestrator-run gate → 2 reviewers (G = CC3/§B-3 metric honesty; H =\n99\tCC6 report-first / no-JSON / crash-safety; **both GO**) → 1 bounded test-hardening\n100\tFIX → re-gate. **Gate: 1120 → 1135 passed** (+16 additive incl. the W3 carryover\n101\ttest below; same 1 pre-existing unrelated `runs` failure, untouched). No\n102\tmigration (0028 reserved for W5); KB read-only.\n103\t\n104\t**CC3/§B-3 (the load-bearing rule) — the surfaced-denominator vanity dodge is\n105\tprovably closed.** `morning_briefing.py::_awareness_metrics` gates useful-find\n106\trate / precision / cost-per-find on **terminal decisions (loaded+dismissed = 7\n107\tlive)**, NOT on surfaced (98). Reviewer G ran the discriminating case\n108\t(surfaced=50 ≥ floor, terminal=7) and the rate stayed suppressed; I added that\n109\texact case as a regression test (`test_rate_gates_on_terminal_decisions_not_\n110\tsurfaced`) so it can't silently regress to surfaced-gating. Every n<30 metric\n111\tsuppresses its rate and shows raw counts + window + sample_size + names the\n112\topen-loop state; floor `AWARENESS_N_FLOOR=30`.\n113\t\n114\t**Delivered:** `_momentum_block` (per-category \"what moved + why it matters\" over\n115\tskills/templates/tools/agents/models; `MOMENTUM_TOP_N=5` hard cap;\n116\t`MOMENTUM_FADE_NIGHTS=3`; \"why\" sourced from `artifacts.interest_why`, kind-\n117\ttemplate fallback). `_value_health_block` (plain-English **RAG + 4 questions** —\n118\tworking? worth it? what's wrong? what to think about? — value-first, zero JSON;\n119\tgreen is structurally unreachable while any signal is open-loop, so the live RAG\n120\tis honestly **AMBER**; \"what to think about\" frames suggestions as\n121\tnon-authoritative per §B-2). Metric set (useful-find rate/OMTM, cost-per-useful-\n122\tfind, precision, frontier-coverage, decisions-influenced, spend-vs-budget) all\n123\tn-gated; frontier-coverage (NULL on live) + decisions-influenced (table absent)\n124\tdegrade to honest \"pending Wave 2/5\", never a fake 0%. New dashboard\n125\t`/api/health/summary` (`{ok, alerts, signals}`, try/except → always 200 on the\n126\tlive KB) with `/api/health/detail` as drill-down. Momentum + value/health ship\n127\tin the morning report AND `build_weekly_note` (CC6 report-first), not\n128\tdashboard-only. Reviewers confirmed zero JSON leaks into John's rendered note.\n129\t\n130\t**Carryover fix:** the W3 BLOCKER-fix regression test (`/api/catalog/models/best`\n131\treturns 200 on a pre-0027 column shape, `_build_models_kb_pre0027`) had been\n132\tadded to `tests/test_dashboard_web.py` but was left UNCOMMITTED by the W3 commit\n133\t(I staged W3 by explicit path and omitted that file). Committed here with W4 so\n134\tthe W3 BLOCKER fix has its committed regression proof. (Process note: stage test\n135\tfiles added by FIX agents, not just the planned set.)\n136\t\n137\t## Wave 3 — Benchmark thin-slice + decision-grade model view — GREEN (2026-06-12)\n138\t\n139\tEXECUTE → orchestrator-run gate → 2 reviewers (E = CC1/CC5 provenance: **GO**;\n140\tF = ingester/composite/cards: **NO-GO**, 1 BLOCKER + 1 MAJOR with a failing\n141\trepro) → FIX →