"pending benchmark data\" (cheap-good/long-context/open-weights\n168\tstill render from price/context/license); route now returns **200** on the live\n169\tKB (orchestrator-verified). (2) `sparse_composite` was correct but **wired into\n170\tnothing** — surfaced it via a `composite` block in the best route + a coverage\n171\t\"k/5\" element in `models.js`. +5 regression tests cover both.\n172\t\n173\t**⚠ ESCALATION → ✅ RESOLVED 2026-06-13 (FALSE ALARM — see the \"RESOLVED\" block\n174\tat the top of this file).** This was a WAL-mode copy artifact, not a real bug;\n175\tthe overnight sweep applied 0026/0027/0028 cleanly and all W2–W5 schema is live.\n176\tThe original (now-superseded) note is kept below for the record:**\n177\t\n178\t**~~⚠ ESCALATION (pre-existing, blocks feature activation in production — NOT\n179\tcaused by this build):~~** `apply_migrations` **fails on the live `kb/aurora.db`**\n180\t(`OperationalError: no such table: helping_hand_log` — an ordering bug in an\n181\tolder migration), so migrations **0026 and 0027 are NOT applied to production**\n182\t(live `model_benchmarks` lacks `source`/`license`; `artifacts` lacks\n183\t`frontier_score`). The live `schema_version` is non-standard (has 3-25 + 31-35,\n184\tmissing 26-30). Every W2/W3 reader degrades gracefully (nothing crashes), but the\n185\tbenchmark + frontier features stay **dormant** until the migration chain is\n186\trepaired. **This needs John's decision** — repairing it touches the live\n187\tproduction DB and is out of a wave's safe scope. W1's model surface is unaffected\n188\t(it added no migration; the `models` table pre-exists). [tracked debt from W2 (b)\n189\t— the benchmark signal that lights up frontier recall — is downstream of this.]\n190\t\n191\t## Wave 2 — Re-aim the collector, behind a shadow — GREEN (2026-06-12)\n192\t\n193\tSame orchestrator loop: EXECUTE → orchestrator-run gate → 2 independent reviewers\n194\t(C = CC2 shadow-safety, D = ranker correctness/§B-1; **both GO**