{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ShZq7rEG7RgyjppcrxtKjQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Discovery Quality & Surfacing (\"water quality\") — Description\n2\t\n3\t**North Star (locked 2026-06-09):** Everything Aurora surfaces to John is correctly classified,\n4\tgenuinely interesting, and worth his attention — a smaller, high-trust catalog with a closed,\n5\tmeasurable value loop — built by evolving the existing pipeline, never touching the proven plumbing.\n6\tPhase 1+2 plumbing (security hardening, cost telemetry, briefing delivery, llm.py upgrades) is done\n7\tand green; this phase is ONLY about what flows through the pipe: classification at ingest, catalog\n8\thygiene, taste-ranked surfacing, and the usage value loop.\n9\t\n10\tSix locked criteria (each wave serves ≥1): (1) right kind at ingest — arxiv never lands as\n11\ttool/agent again, vendor posts and pointer rows never become tools, OpenRouter is a reference table;\n12\t(2) top finds are named, ranked, eligible artifacts with a why-line — never raw IDs; (3) a persisted\n13\tinterest (taste) score drives ranking; (4) productivity derives from real `hh_events` usage and\n14\tusage feeds back into ranking; (5) the catalog is trustworthy — noise backfilled, dupes merged,\n15\tstale entries retire on policy, counts honest; (6) Wave 1 changes the next morning's briefing, the\n16\tweekly digest ships early.\n17\t\n18\tUser gate decisions (locked): papers = opt-in stream (`kind='paper'`; never pushed; \"papers worth\n19\treading\" in the weekly digest; matchable in HH pull queries, labeled — D2); vendor blog posts\n20\trejected at ingest; taste scorer approved at cents/night (metered, capped); HH model rows excluded\n21\tfrom single-mode routing + surfaced-telemetry but recallable in ranked/compare (D1).\n22\t\n23\t## Success criteria\n24\t- The morning session_note contains zero raw IDs; every top find is a named, eligible (GitHub-hosted\n25\t  or badged, never `local:`) artifact with a one-line why and a quality signal when discriminating.\n26\t- A standing noise audit returns 0 (no arxiv-as-tool/agent, no vendor-blog tools, no pointer\n27\t  artifacts, no dead library links, no retired rows in serving surfaces).\n28\t- Every new find carries `interest_score` + `interest_why`, scored against `docs/INTEREST_PROFILE.md`,\n29\t  metered at a non-zero priced rate, capped nightly.\n30\t- `productivity_index` = per-query suggestion adoption from `hh_events` (window labeled, sample size\n31\t  shown); usage (loaded/dismissed) demonstrably shifts ranking via a bounded modifier.\n32\t- The weekly digest ships on schedule with ranked finds, the papers stream, and catalog-health deltas.\n33\t- Locked-preserved intact: KB schema (additive migrations only) + browsable library, single-owner\n34\t  security gate, deterministic cost telemetry, Helping Hand MCP + publisher.\n35\t\n36\t## Hard constraints\n37\t- Evolve, don't rebuild (researchPrime AuroraTwo verdict). No discovery-engine parallelism. Issue #5\n38\t  (H1 fetch reliability) is out of scope.\n39\t- Backfills re-kind/retire ONLY — never DELETE rows; `--dry-run` + `--audit-out` mandatory on every\n40\t  backfill; `bin/migrate_to_kind_paper.py`'s delete step must never run again (it would delete 3\n41\t  legitimate local skills, ids 822-824).\n42\t- Library is a filesystem surface: any re-kind/retire owns the page moves + `regenerate_indexes`;\n43\t  the publisher must never ship retired pages (predicate must evaluate BEFORE the\n44\t  `AURORA_SECURITY_MODE` early-return at `publisher.py:78-79`).\n45\t- Scheduled tasks execute `C:\\dev\\aurora` directly (the working tree IS production; sweeps at\n46\t  01:07/02:19/03:41/05:03, briefing 06:47): every wave ends with a clean committed tree.\n47\t- Any wave touching `helping-hand-plugin/mcp-servers/aurora-kb/server.py` ends with plugin rebuild\n48\t  (`bin/build-plugin.py`) + reinstall + live smoke — the runtime is the installed plugin, not the repo.\n49\t- test-command: `python -m pytest`. 915-test baseline stays green; no test weakening; the count may\n50\t  only rise.\n51\t\n52\t## Provenance\n53\tMaster plan (Crucible Stage 1, two Shark-Tank rounds + independent Judge, user-approved 2026-06-09):\n54\t`docs/AURORA_DISCOVERY_QUALITY_PLAN.md` — evidence base E1–E23 all code/DB-grounded. Stage-2\n55\tverification (HH scorer seam, stars budget, dupe set, source-gate false positives, drain-path seam)\n56\tcompleted 2026-06-09 and folded into the waves below.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01D3vS1XSt6PQR86K5UNE1p5","session_id":"0e9f13f6-4032-41a4-8d9f-b9e18c221609","uuid":"615834a0-0985-42aa-b4c8-bd46ae11df06","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:39:54.380Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore discovery quality + value"}
