{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Af8kUs7edngfzpfJMDAhtQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora — No-Hallucination Guardrails for Pricing Adjudication\n2\t\n3\t**Date:** 2026-05-25\n4\t**Trigger:** Claude Opus 4.6 hallucination incident, nights of 2026-05-24/25\n5\t**Authors:** Deep-Think / Deep-Research / Expert-Coder parallel agents + curator review\n6\t**Status:** MVP landed (this commit); full quorum redesign scheduled — see `docs/NEXT_STEPS.md`\n7\t\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t## The incident\n11\t\n12\tOn 2026-05-24 and 2026-05-25 the morning briefing flagged Anthropic's Claude Opus 4.6 with:\n13\t\n14\t- **Source A** (OpenRouter `/v1/models` JSON): $5 / MTok input, $25 / MTok output\n15\t- **Source B** (Gemini Flash, asked to \"recall current pricing from training\"): $15 / MTok input, $75 / MTok output\n16\t- **Adjudicator** (Sonnet 4.6, asked \"which is correct?\"): declared $15/$75 the verified real-world price with 88-99% confidence; wrote four paragraphs of plausible rationale (\"Source A must be stale or a promotional tier\")\n17\t- **Reality** (verified via WebSearch + [Anthropic's own pricing page](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing) + [pricepertoken.com tracker](https://pricepertoken.com/pricing-page/model/anthropic-claude-opus-4.6)): **$5 / $25 — Source A was correct all along**\n18\t\n19\tThe OpenRouter row was right. The LLM-recall \"Source B\" was a hallucination matching old Opus-3 pricing. The Sonnet adjudicator rubber-stamped the hallucination because the prompt asked it to \"decide which is more likely\" rather than \"fetch and verify.\"\n20\t\n21\t**Blast radius:** Limited this time. The slug mismatch (`claude-opus-latest` in the debate vs `claude-opus-4-6` in `kb/pricing.yaml`) prevented `sync_to_pricing_yaml` from propagating the wrong value to the CostRecorder's billing source. **`kb/pricing.yaml` still has the correct $5/$25.** But the architecture was one slug-alias coincidence away from a 3x cost-billing inflation across every Aurora sweep.\n22\t\n23\t---\n24\t\n25\t## Root cause (deep-think)\n26\t\n27\tNine load-bearing assumptions in `roles/pricing_collector.py` were all wrong:\n28\t\n29\t1. The market_research LLM has accurate, recent training data for pricing.\n30\t2. Sonnet's rationale prose correlates with truth.\n31\t3. A confidence float emitted by an LLM means anything.\n32\t4. Disagreement implies Source A is the side that's wrong.\n33\t5. \"Opus is expensive\" prior > fresh aggregator number.\n34\t6. The two sources are independent (both were LLMs).\n35\t7. The 5%-divergence band gated *whether to debate*, but nothing gated *whether to accept the debate's verdict*.\n36\t8. The `is_volatile` (>2x) flag was logged but never blocked.\n37\t9. A debate verdict was safe to mirror into the global `pricing.yaml` that CostRecorder reads.\n38\t\n39\tThe Bucket O wave A fix (O-4) removed a forced *test* trigger but left the structural defect untouched: **the debate has no sourced inputs and writes to the cost source-of-truth.** Bucket O treated this as a cost regression. It is a correctness regression.\n40\t\n41\t---\n42\t\n43\t## MVP guardrails (landed this commit)\n44\t\n45\tThree invariants now hold in `roles/pricing_collector.py`:\n46\t\n47\t### G1. URL-citation required\n48\t\n49\t`DEBATE_PROMPT` rewritten to demand a real, fetchable `source_url` field. The model is told its `verified_price_*` fields are *advisory*; the verifier ignores them when the URL doesn't render those prices. If the model returns `source_url=\"\"`, the system logs `accepted=0, reason=\"no_citation\"` and **keeps the aggregator price**.\n50\t\n51\t### G2. Deterministic fetch-and-grep verification\n52\t\n53\tNew `verify_citation(source_url, claimed_in, claimed_out)`:\n54\t\n55\t```python\n56\thttpx.get(url, timeout=10s, follow_redirects=True,\n57\t          headers={\"User-Agent\": \"Aurora-PricingVerifier/1.0 ...\"})\n58\t→ trafilatura.extract() (fallback: BeautifulSoup → raw HTML)\n59\t→ regex set against $X/M, $X/MTok, $X per million, $X/1K (×1000)\n60\t→ both claimed prices must appear within ±$0.005 tolerance\n61\t→ (True, snippet) | (False, reason)\n62\t```\n63\t\n64\t**No LLM in this path.** Any LLM-proposed price without a verified citation routes to `pricing_history` with `accepted=0` — never to `pricing.yaml` or the `models` satellite table.\n65\t\n66\t### G3. Kill-switch with default `dry-run` mode\n67\t\n68\tEnv `AURORA_PRICING_DEBATE_MODE`:\n69\t\n70\t- `disabled` — function exits immediately (operator emergency button)\n71\t- `dry-run` (default for the first 3 nights) — runs the full path, writes proposals to `pricing_history` with `accepted=0`, **never touches `pricing.yaml` or `models`**\n72\t- `live` — writes only on verified citations\n73\t\n74\tOperator promotes to `live` after spot-checking 3 nights of `pricing_history` rows.\n75\t\n76\t### Audit table — `kb/migrations/0006_pricing_history.sql`\n77\t\n78\t```sql\n79\tCREATE TABLE pricing_history (\n80\t    id, model_artifact_id, run_id,\n81\t    old_price_in, old_price_out, new_price_in, new_price_out,\n82\t    source_urls_json, citation_count, adjudicator_model,\n83\t    accepted (0|1), reason, mode, recorded_at\n84\t);\n85\t```\n86\t\n87\tEvery proposal — accepted, rejected, or dry-run — persists here. Rolling back a bad night is `SELECT … WHERE accepted=1 AND recorded_at > X` followed by reverting from `old_price_*`.\n88\t\n89\t### Sanity prior (G3 lite)\n90\t\n91\t`is_volatile` (proposed >2× or <0.5× aggregator) is still computed but now feeds into the `pricing_watch.md` status column with a `⚠ HIGH` marker. The full quorum design (next section) promotes this to a hard gate requiring a third citation.\n92\t\n93\t---\n94\t\n95\t## Tests landed\n96\t\n97\t`tests/test_pricing_guardrails.py` — 14 tests, all green:\n98\t\n99\t- `verify_citation` happy path + URL invalid + URL 404 + URL fetch-fail + price not on page + `$X/1K` normalization\n100\t- `default_mode_is_dry_run` — even with a verified citation, no DB/YAML write\n101\t- `disabled_mode_exits_immediately` — `market_research` never called\n102\t- **`test_regression_opus_46_hallucination_rejected`** — *the* test that pins the bug: given `verify_citation` returning False (URL exists but doesn't render $15/$75), DB stays at $5/$25 and `pricing_history.accepted=0` with `reason='verify_failed:...'`\n103\t- `no_source_url_logs_no_citation_rejection`\n104\t- `live_mode_writes_only_on_verified_citation`\n105\t- `invalid_mode_falls_back_to_dry_run`\n106\t\n107\t---\n108\t\n109\t## Full quorum redesign (scheduled, not yet landed)\n110\t\n111\tThe MVP closes the hole — it makes the failure case *visible* and *reversible* without preventing the system from doing useful work. The full redesign upgrades to a quorum-of-deterministic-sources pattern researched by the parallel deep-research agent.\n112\t\n113\t### Design (Sources A through D)\n114\t\n115\t| Source | Type | Cost | Confidence weight |\n116\t|---|---|---|---|\n117\t| **A — OpenRouter `/v1/models`** | JSON, deterministic | $0 | 1.0 |\n118\t| **B — Anthropic web_search_20260209 tool** | LLM grounded with snippets | ~$0.04/model | 0.5 default, → 1.0 if citation passes G2 |\n119\t| **C — models.dev `api.json`** | JSON, deterministic | $0 | 1.0 |\n120\t| **D — LiteLLM `model_prices_and_context_window.json`** | JSON, deterministic | $0 | 1.0 |\n121\t\n122\tAcceptance rule: **≥3 of 4 weighted sources agree within 5%** AND B's cited URL passes G2 verification → accept. Otherwise: log to `pricing_history` and surface in morning briefing for operator review.\n123\t\n124\tSources referenced in the agent research:\n125\t\n126\t- [Anthropic web_search tool docs](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/docs/agents-and-tools/tool-use/web-search-tool) — only major API that returns `cited_text` snippet (≤150 chars) in the response payload, exactly what G2 needs\n127\t- [models.dev api.json](https://models.dev/api.json) — community-maintained structured JSON with input/output/cache_read/cache_write/context_over_200k\n128\t- [LiteLLM cost calc](https://deepwiki.com/BerriAI/litellm/2.6-cost-calculation-and-model-pricing) — 2,600+ models, daily-updated, drives tokencost.dev\n129\t- [SemanticCite (arXiv 2511.16198)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.16198) — Nov 2025 OSS pipeline for the claim-extractor → retriever → matcher → reasoner pattern\n130\t- [RIKER 172B-token study (arXiv 2603.08274v1)](https://arxiv.org/html/2603.08274v1) — March 2026 LLM-as-judge factuality study; concludes LLM judges are biased on factual tasks and recommends ground-truth-first deterministic scoring\n131\t- [TTS multi-source incentive-aligned (arXiv 2509.25184)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.25184) — Feb 2026 update; quorum with peer-prediction source weighting\n132\t- [Council Mode (arXiv 2604.02923)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.02923) — 35.9% hallucination reduction on HaluEval via heterogeneous parallel models + structured synthesis\n133\t\n134\t### Scope (to land in 2026-05-28 → 06-04 window per NEXT_STEPS.md)\n135\t\n136\t1. **Grounded source B** — extend `aurora.llm.call_anthropic` to accept a `tools=[{\"type\":\"web_search_20260209\", \"name\":\"web_search\", \"max_uses\":4, \"allowed_domains\":[...provider domains...]}]` kwarg. Parse the `web_search_result_location` blocks for `cited_text` snippets per claim.\n137\t2. **Add JSON sources C + D** — daily fetch + cache of `models.dev/api.json` and the LiteLLM JSON. Commit the snapshot files for reproducibility.\n138\t3. **Quorum decision** in `run_verification`: replace the single-citation acceptance with a multi-source agreement check + sanity-prior 3-citation requirement on >2× divergence.\n139\t4. **Migrate `models` and `pricing.yaml` writes** to require quorum acceptance, not just G2 verification.\n140\t5. **Morning briefing surfacing** — extend `morning_briefing.py` with a `pricing_proposals` block summarizing dry-run / accepted / rejected rows from `pricing_history`.\n141\t\n142\tEstimated effort: 6-10 hours including the migration to grounded web search in `llm.py`.\n143\t\n144\t---\n145\t\n146\t## Operator behavior tomorrow morning\n147\t\n148\tIf the MVP guardrail behaves as expected (next nightly sweep at 02:00 PT):\n149\t\n150\t1. The pricing_collector runs in **dry-run** mode by default (until you promote via env).\n151\t2. The morning briefing's `## 💰 Pricing Watch` section now shows three states per row: ✅ **ACCEPTED** (live + verified — won't appear until you set `AURORA_PRICING_DEBATE_MODE=live`), 🚫 **REJECTED** (citation didn't verify), 🔍 **DRY-RUN** (would have been applied in live mode).\n152\t3. `kb/pricing.yaml` stays untouched. `models` satellite stays untouched. `CostRecorder` keeps billing against the OpenRouter-sourced prices.\n153\t4. `pricing_history` accumulates one row per debated model per night — review for 3 nights, then `setx AURORA_PRICING_DEBATE_MODE live` to promote.\n154\t5. The Opus 4.6 row, if it's debated again, will log `accepted=0 reason=\"verify_failed:...\"` because Sonnet's fabricated $15/$75 doesn't appear at https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing. The right answer ($5/$25) stays.\n155\t\n156\t---\n157\t\n158\t## Files touched this commit\n159\t\n160\t- `roles/pricing_collector.py` — rewritten (~310 LOC) with verify_citation, kill-switch, mode handling, audit-log integration\n161\t- `kb/migrations/0006_pricing_history.sql` — new (~30 LOC)\n162\t- `tests/test_pricing_guardrails.py` — new (~290 LOC, 14 tests)\n163\t- `docs/PRICING_GUARDRAILS.md` — this file\n164\t- `docs/NEXT_STEPS.md` — entry added for the full quorum redesign\n165\t\n166\t**Total: ~700 LOC including tests + docs. Tests: 149/149 green (135 baseline + 14 new).**\n167\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01D3vS1XSt6PQR86K5UNE1p5","session_id":"0e9f13f6-4032-41a4-8d9f-b9e18c221609","uuid":"7572d094-89e4-47bc-83b5-7c6c35952e62","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:40:16.422Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore discovery quality + value"}
