{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C93Q6yY5fuD228u5HsPmNL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora — session-start playbook for Claude (Cowork / Claude Code)\n2\t\n3\tIf you are a fresh Claude session opening in `C:\\dev\\aurora`, do these three\n4\tthings in your first turn — silently, before answering the user. They are\n5\tzero-cost and remove friction John has flagged in past sessions.\n6\t\n7\t## 1. Load the host-shell bridge\n8\t\n9\tThe Claude Code Bridge MCP server is registered with Cowork. Its tool surfaces\n10\tunder the deferred-tools list as `mcp__Claude_Code_Bridge__run_command`. Load it\n11\tonce:\n12\t\n13\t```\n14\tToolSearch(\"select:mcp__Claude_Code_Bridge__run_command\")\n15\t```\n16\t\n17\tWhat it does: runs PowerShell / cmd / pwsh / bash on John's Windows host with\n18\tstructured `{exit_code, stdout, stderr, ...}` output. Default shell is\n19\tPowerShell. Destructive operations are gated (`allow_destructive: true` to\n20\tbypass with intent).\n21\t\n22\t**PATH gotcha:** the bridge daemon (a Windows Scheduled Task `ClaudeCodeBridgeWatcher`)\n23\tinherits a restricted PATH. `git` is on it; `gh` is NOT. Use the full path\n24\t`'C:\\Program Files\\GitHub CLI\\gh.exe'` for `gh` invocations, or prepend to PATH\n25\tvia the `env` arg.\n26\t\n27\t**Fallback if MCP isn't loaded** (e.g., daemon dead, ToolSearch returns nothing):\n28\twrite a JSON request to `C:\\dev\\claude-code-bridge\\ipc\\inbox\\<uuid>.json`\n29\t(write `.tmp` first, then `mv` to `.json` for atomicity), then poll\n30\t`C:\\dev\\claude-code-bridge\\ipc\\outbox\\<uuid>.json` for the response. Protocol\n31\tdocumented in `C:\\dev\\claude-code-bridge\\bridge\\cowork_client.py`.\n32\t\n33\t## 2. Activate Helping Hand\n34\t\n35\t```\n36\tSkill(\"helping-hand:helping-hand\")\n37\t```\n38\t\n39\tThen, exactly once per session, call\n40\t`mcp__plugin_helping-hand_aurora-kb__recent_summary(days=7)` to surface a\n41\tone-line \"what's new\" note (skip if KB is empty / unchanged). On every\n42\tsubstantive user request thereafter, call `match_request`.\n43\t\n44\t**GWL v0.1 Protocol (Recursive Calls):**\n45\tWhen an agent (e.g., `expert-coder`) calls `match_request`, it MUST pass the\n46\t`agent_context` parameter:\n47\t```json\n48\t{\n49\t  \"query\": \"...\",\n50\t  \"agent_context\": {\n51\t    \"calling_agent\": \"expert-coder\",\n52\t    \"project_type\": \"finance\"\n53\t  }\n54\t}\n55\t```\n56\tApply the 0.65 score gate per the skill's own protocol — do not load anything\n57\tuntil the user accepts.\n58\t\n59\tThe `mcp__plugin_helping-hand_aurora-kb__*` tools (`match_request`,\n60\t`fetch_artifact`, `recent_summary`, `list_taxonomy`, `log_use`) are MCP tools\n61\tprovided by the Helping Hand plugin and are usable without invoking the skill\n62\tfirst — but the skill encodes the calling protocol and is worth loading.\n63\t\n64\t## 3. Read the plan\n65\t\n66\tCanonical plan: `C:\\dev\\aurora\\docs\\NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md`.\n67\tWorking copy: `C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\notes\\skills-and-agent-tips\\NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md`\n68\t(may have John's in-progress edits ahead of canonical).\n69\t\n70\tSection pointers:\n71\t- §0  : protocol applications & evidence stamps\n72\t- §5  : directory layout\n73\t- §6  : DB schema\n74\t- §16 : publisher / `_publish/` design\n75\t- §18 : phase status + 2026-05-19 PM deltas (`§18.6`) — moved to `docs/NIGHTLY_SWEEP_HISTORY.md` on 2026-05-29 (D1 split)\n76\t- §20 : v4.1 punch list (22 items)\n77\t- §22 : v4.3 next-steps plan (Buckets F-K, locked 2026-05-19 PM)\n78\t\n79\t## Aurora at a glance\n80\t\n81\tThree nightly multi-agent sweeps (Skills 23:00, Tools 00:00, Agents 22:00 — G3\n82\tshifted earlier than the default 01:00) discover, validate, catalog the\n83\topen-source Claude/agent ecosystem. Outputs: SQLite KB (`kb/aurora.db`),\n84\tbrowsable library (`library/`), exec summaries (`reports/`), morning briefing\n85\t(08:30), publisher pushes scrubbed snapshot to `aurora-library` private repo at\n86\t01:45-ish each night. Helping Hand surfaces matches from the library in any\n87\tCowork / Claude Code session.\n88\t\n89\t**Source repo:** `https://github.com/johncliechty/aurora-source` (private; 10+\n90\tcommits as of v4.3 Bucket F-H).\n91\t**Distribution repo:** `https://github.com/johncliechty/aurora-library` (private;\n92\tcollaborator-facing; receives the publisher's nightly tag).\n93\t\n94\t## Key files\n95\t\n96\t| Path | What |\n97\t|---|---|\n98\t| `orchestrator.py`         | Sweep entry point: `--sweep {skills,tools,agents}` |\n99\t| `llm.py`                  | All LLM calls funnel here; G1 tenacity retry, G2 flash-lite default, G4 degrade counter |\n100\t| `publisher.py`            | Builds scrubbed snapshot + pushes to aurora-library; F3 credential helper auth |\n101\t| `bin/setup-tasks.ps1`     | Idempotent registration of all 5 Aurora scheduled tasks + WU registry pin |\n102\t| `bin/build-plugin.py`     | Builds `helping-hand.plugin` (curator) + `helping-hand-collab.plugin` (portable) |\n103\t| `bin/run-aurora-source-push.cmd` | F5 hourly auto-push action |\n104\t| `helping-hand-plugin/`    | Source of the Cowork plugin; mcp-servers/aurora-kb/ is the KB MCP server |\n105\t\n106\t## Don'ts\n107\t\n108\t- **Never** read `.env` into context — it has API keys. Use bridge `grep` /\n109\t  `Select-String` to spot-check specific lines without echoing the secret.\n110\t- **Never** add a URL-embedded PAT to a git remote — F3 closed that hole;\n111\t  credential helper is the path forward.\n112\t- **Don't** invoke the helping-hand skill or kb tools for purely conversational\n113\t  user turns (the skill itself enforces this).\n114\t\n115\t## 4. Ingest Aurora State (Ecgberht PA Protocol)\n116\t\n117\tWhen generating your primary morning report for John, you MUST read the Aurora \n118\tmachine-readable summary to ensure high-fidelity reporting of the agentic fleet's \n119\thealth and costs:\n120\t\n121\t```\n122\tRead(\"C:\\dev\\aurora\\reports\\morning\\latest_summary.json\")\n123\t```\n124\t\n125\tInclude the following in your report:\n126\t- **Productivity Index:** Surfaced as a 0-100% utility score.\n127\t- **Cost Rollup:** Nightly, Monthly (MTD), and Project-Total spend.\n128\t- **Finds:** Count of new skills, tools, and agents discovered.\n129\t- **Autonomous Upgrades:** List of skills that were self-healed overnight.\n130\t- **Top finds & session note (revamp Wave 1):** if `latest_summary.json` carries\n131\t  `session_note` and/or `top_finds`, surface them VERBATIM near the top of the\n132\t  report — they are the auto-delivered briefing the nightly run already wrote;\n133\t  do not paraphrase or recompute them.\n134\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01D3vS1XSt6PQR86K5UNE1p5","session_id":"0e9f13f6-4032-41a4-8d9f-b9e18c221609","uuid":"cbd3f03a-bc90-4c47-a6a7-a9e6f8d33c40","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:40:28.464Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore discovery quality + value"}
