{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VS4dKX54KHN488GY9Zrs2d","type":"tool_result","content":"151:def lookup_cache_rates(pricing: dict, vendor: str, model: str) -> tuple[float, float]:\n152:    \"\"\"Resolve (cache_read_rate, cache_write_rate) per-million USD for vendor/model.\n154:    Wave L1 (2026-06-07): prompt-caching sub-rates. cache_read bills ~0.1x input,\n155:    cache_write (cache-creation) ~1.25x input (5-min ephemeral TTL). Mirrors\n157:    behaviour. A model priced for in/out but WITHOUT cache sub-rates returns\n158:    (0.0, 0.0) here (and warns once) — so cache tokens on an un-cache-priced\n160:    legacy callers never pass cache tokens, so this is never consulted for them.\n169:            cr = r.get(\"cache_read_per_million_usd\")\n170:            cw = r.get(\"cache_write_per_million_usd\")\n173:            break  # model priced for in/out but no cache sub-rates\n174:    tag = f\"cache:{vendor}/{model}\"\n177:        log.warning(\"pricing: no cache sub-rate for %s/%s — recording cache tokens \"\n178:                    \"at $0.0 (add cache_read_per_million_usd / \"\n179:                    \"cache_write_per_million_usd to kb/pricing.yaml)\", vendor, model)\n247:def batch_discount(pricing: dict) -> float:\n252:        return float(pricing.get(\"batch_discount\", 1.0))\n267:               cache_read_tokens: int = 0, cache_write_tokens: int = 0,\n268:               batch_mode: bool = False) -> float:\n273:        cache terms are 0 and the batch multiplier is 1.0 — the usd_estimate and\n274:        every column written are exactly as before (cache_read_tokens /\n275:        cache_write_tokens land NULL, batch_mode 0).\n277:        Wave L1 (2026-06-07): when supplied, `cache_read_tokens` /\n278:        `cache_write_tokens` are priced at the per-model cache sub-rates\n279:        (cache_read ~0.1x input, cache_write ~1.25x input) ON TOP of the regular\n280:        input/output spend, and `batch_mode=True` applies the top-level\n281:        `batch_discount` multiplier (~0.5x) to the WHOLE usd_estimate (the\n282:        Batches API discounts cache spend too). cache_read_tokens are billed\n284:        non-cached input only (the Anthropic usage shape splits them).\n297:        if cache_read_tokens or cache_write_tokens:\n298:            cache_read_rate, cache_write_rate = lookup_cache_rates(self.pricing, vendor, model)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01UkhjqCpsBaWTEbkLkiiJeJ","session_id":"0e9f13f6-4032-41a4-8d9f-b9e18c221609","uuid":"8b7e1e01-95c4-4f5c-82ff-cad4a6652e6a","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:40:33.011Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore Aurora core architecture"}
