{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019yinPhBqtj4zz7WeVeNdaj","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have enough information to construct the comprehensive report. Let me synthesize the findings:\n\n---\n\n## AURORA PROJECT: STRATEGY & CURRENT DIRECTION — RIGOROUS ASSESSMENT\n\n---\n\n### **1. NORTH STAR: STATED PURPOSE & EVOLUTION**\n\n**Original (v1, May 2026, from NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md §1):**\n> \"Three independent multi-agent sweeps run every night against the open-source ecosystem and produce a curated, queryable knowledge base... Outputs: SQLite KB, browsable library, nightly exec summaries, 08:30 morning briefing, and a `helping-hand` plugin.\"\n\n**Revamped (June 6, 2026, AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md North Star, locked):**\n> \"Make Aurora deliver **felt, trustworthy value** *and* run on a **robust Foreman/Crucible-style agentic architecture** — as **co-equal goals**.\" *(Line 10–13: emphasis on VALUE as co-equal with architecture.)*\n\n**Further refined (June 11, 2026, HANDOFF.md §1, John's verbatim intent, now locked for awareness revamp):**\n> \"Aurora exists to **make John aware of all current advances in agentic AI** — agentic systems, theories, approaches, advances in **harnesses**, the **models** that feed them, the **benchmarks**, and new **skills / templates / tools**. This serves THREE jobs, co-equal: (1) **Educate John**, (2) **Guide generation of new agents**, (3) **Feed the agentic systems** — make all of it available to the GWL agentic system, to Claude (via Helping Hand), and to Gemini for retrieval.\"\n\n**CRITICAL TENSION IDENTIFIED:** The original v1 purpose (\"discover, validate, catalog the open-source Claude/agent ecosystem\") was **discovery-centric**. By June 11, the North Star shifted to **awareness + decision-instrument + agent-feeding**. John explicitly said (HANDOFF.md §2, reaction C): *the system should inform \"should I adopt this?\"* — a decision-guiding purpose, not just discovery. The revamp's adversarial research (§B-3 of RESEARCH.md) flagged: \"the polish is working against honesty: it looks finished, so value is assumed that isn't there.\"\n\n---\n\n### **2. WAVES ACROSS TWO CONCURRENT REVAMPS**\n\n#### **A. Aurora Revamp (Crucible/Foreman-driven, June 6 onward)**\nStated in AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md:\n\n| Wave | Deliverable | Status | Quote |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **0** | Re-light Helping Hand (fix thresholds) | ✅ DONE (2026-06-06) | \"Verified 2026-06-06: `recent_summary` responded live in-session (KB returns counts), so the server is enabled and reachable.\" (Line 62–63) |\n| **1** | Make output visible (briefing notify, library index join) | 🟡 In scope, not confirmed done | \"Acceptance: Given a completed nightly sweep, When briefing runs, Then John receives a notification... And `library/index.md` shows real domains/complexity for ≥95% of placed artifacts.\" (Line 73) |\n| **2** | Security-gate single-owner + backfill | 🟡 In scope | De-duplicate `gate_predicate_sql()`, backfill `security_status` (Line 77–84). |\n| **3** | Evidence-rigor fix-loop + confidence badge | 🟡 In scope | EXECUTE→REVIEW→FIX→RE-REVIEW loop with `verified | documented | lossy` badge (Line 86–103). |\n| **4** | Trustworthy cost numbers | 🟡 In scope | Replace UNVERIFIED guesses in `pricing.yaml` with real rates (Line 105–112). |\n| **5** | Scout memory / source-reputation | 🟡 In scope | Track per-source yield, prioritize high-yield sources (Line 114–124). |\n| — | Judgment fan-out (parallel evaluation) | ❌ DEFERRED behind tripwire | \"Deferred behind a tripwire... until `AURORA_SWARM_TOP_K ≥ ~20`\" (Line 128–135). |\n\n**Status stamp:** Lines 4–5 state \"Stage 0 (North Star locked) ✅ · Stage 1 (Master Plan, converged) ✅ · Stage 2 (this doc) — wave decomposition for Foreman handoff.\" *No waves are marked EXECUTED — they are specification, not yet built.*\n\n#### **B. Aurora Awareness Revamp (Crucible/Foreman-driven, June 11–13 onward)**\nExplicit parallel effort, from HANDOFF.md §0: \"carry John's thinking + grounded facts into a FRESH Claude Code session that runs **researchPrime** (to gather outside ideas) and then **Crucible** (to re-plan the Aurora dashboard AND the backend collection/curation).\"\n\nStatus per EXECUTION-LOG.md lines 9–21:\n\n| Wave | Intent | Status | Test count |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **1** | Surface 352 already-collected models | ✅ GREEN (2026-06-12) | 1076→1089 (+13 tests) |\n| **2** | Re-aim collector toward harnesses (shadow-only) | ✅ GREEN (2026-06-12) | 1089→1108 (+19 tests) |\n| **3** | Benchmark thin-slice (Epoch CC-BY) + decision view | ✅ GREEN (2026-06-12, w/ W3 false-alarm correction 2026-06-13) | 1108→1120 (+12 tests) |\n| **4** | Awareness \"what moved\" + plain-English value/health | ✅ GREEN (2026-06-12) | 1120→1135 (+16 tests) |\n| **5** | Minimal adoption (decisions table + capture) | ✅ GREEN (2026-06-12) | 1135→1152 (+17 tests) |\n\n**Status stamp (lines 17–20):** \"PROJECT COMPLETE — all 5 waves GREEN (2026-06-12). Test baseline 1076 → **1152 passed** (+76 additive; the lone failing `test_no_stale_running_runs_from_yesterday` is a pre-existing, unrelated live-DB stale-`runs` artifact present before W1, left untouched per CC4).\"\n\n**Critical note (lines 22–46):** On 2026-06-13, a \"live-DB migration breakage\" was **IDENTIFIED AS A FALSE ALARM** — root cause was diagnosing a WAL-mode SQLite DB by copying only the `.db` file (omitting `-wal`). The real DB was healthy; migrations `0026/0027/0028` were applied by the overnight sweep. **All W2–W5 schema is live.**\n\n---\n\n### **3. EVIDENCE QUALITY & VERIFICATION STATUS**\n\n#### **Revamp 1 (Core Aurora Revamp)**\n- **Waves 0–5 are SPECIFIED, not BUILT.** AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md is a plan for Foreman execution, not a deployment report.\n- **Status language:** \"Wave 0 — Re-light Helping Hand ✅ DONE\" is marked complete because a small manual threshold fix was applied and tested. Waves 1–5 are framed as specification (\"Done-when\", Given/When/Then acceptance criteria) — no execution log, no commit hash, no live verification.\n- **Risk:** The plan was \"forged via Crucible\" (Crucible Stage 2, line 4) with adversarial review, but there is **no evidence of Foreman execution yet**. No commits trace back to this plan's waves (beyond Wave 0). The repo's `git log` shows no work-in-progress branches for waves 1–5.\n\n#### **Revamp 2 (Awareness Revamp) — VERIFICATION EVIDENCE**\n- **Research-backed:** researchPrime report (RESEARCH.md) ran with \"adversarial pass: RAN — 2 heterogeneous reviewers (≥2-agree) + context-free judge/synthesizer\" (line 3). Corrections in §B are labeled \"BINDING on the plan.\"\n- **Crucible-planned:** Stage 0 (North Star locked, 2026-06-11) + Stage 1 (Master Plan approved 2026-06-12, referenced in DESCRIPTION.md line 15) + Stage 2 (IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md, Foreman-ready).\n- **Foreman-executed:** All 5 waves GREEN with commit hashes, test deltas (+76 additive tests, final count 1152), and reviewer sign-offs. Execution-log names the reviewers: (W1: J, C / W2: D, C / W3: E, F / W4: G, H / W5: I, J) and stamps each wave with \"both GO\" or identifies BLOCKERs + fixes.\n- **False alarm resolved:** The \"live-DB migration breakage\" (escalation in lines 173–189, marked as a pre-rollback WAL-copy artifact) was verified RESOLVED on 2026-06-13 by confirming the overnight sweep applied all migrations cleanly (line 34: \"live `schema_version` now holds 26, 27, 28\").\n- **One pre-existing unrelated failure:** `test_no_stale_running_runs_from_yesterday` is a live-DB artifact unrelated to the revamp work; left untouched per constraint CC4 (line 20–21).\n\n**Verdict:** Awareness revamp is **SHIPPED & VERIFIED**. The Core Aurora Revamp waves 1–5 are PLANNED but not executed.\n\n---\n\n### **4. JOHN'S NEEDS & SINGLE-USER NATURE**\n\n**Who is John? (Inferred from docs)**\n- Single operator, single user (NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md §17: \"Initial collaborators | John only for v1\").\n- Works in two primary projects: Aurora (discovery/curation) and Agentic-Home / Ghost World Labs (GWL — agent-building). Aurora feeds both his awareness and the GWL agent systems.\n- Uses Claude Code / Cowork as his primary interface; Gemini as a secondary agent; Windows host with Task Scheduler as the cron.\n\n**Friction John flagged (HANDOFF.md §2):**\n| # | Reaction | Real ask |\n|---|---|---|\n| B | \"Nothing new last night but we still spent money.\" | **Honest value accounting:** what did the spend buy? Is it finding things worth the money? |\n| C | Suggested adoption — is this something I act on? | Make adoption **actionable**: a review tab with human-readable summary, risks, advantages, **why adopt / why not**. |\n| D | **Health page: \"completely not helpful… looks like something a computer might read.\"** | **Human-readable health + value:** plain-English \"is it working, is it worth it, what's wrong, what should I think about.\" |\n| E | What was new — wants it **by category** + **models + pricing** + \"am I actually collecting anything?\" | A **category intelligence** surface: per-category \"what's the current best-in-class + what's newly notable,\" not a raw nightly dump. |\n| F | Catalog map: not interested. Wants a **knowledge / relationship map**. | A **human-readable relationship map** of the agentic-AI landscape — how systems relate — not a taxonomy. |\n\n**The existential complaint (RESEARCH.md §C, lines 93–95):**\n> \"Stripped of framing, a night delivers 8-21 arxiv papers + ~20 rejections to a polished read-only dashboard; last night produced **zero** skills/tools/agents. The system built to track harnesses/models/benchmarks/skills spent its dollar on the one category John mentioned in passing.\"\n\n**Value asymmetry (RESEARCH.md §B-3, lines 75–77):**\n> \"Live `hh_events`: 106 events but only **n=7 carry a decision** (6 loaded, 1 dismissed) across 21 queries / 10 sessions / 3 weeks... show raw counts; the plan must explicitly name that until usage exists, every learned/derived signal (taste, precision, ring) runs **open-loop**.\"\n\n---\n\n### **5. EXPLICIT TENSIONS & UNRESOLVED DECISIONS**\n\n#### **A. Architecture vs. Value — Co-equal or Sequential?**\n**Tension:** AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md (June 6) locked \"felt, trustworthy value *and* robust architecture — **as co-equal goals**\" (line 10–13). However, the reframe (lines 33–46) revealed that \"~70% of the felt pain is an unwired 'consume' loop + config bugs, not the discovery engine.\" The decision: **Wave 0 re-lights Helping Hand; Waves 1–5 are thin-vertical, putting the *consume* half (visibility, adoption, value accounting) first, not the discovery swarm.** This inverts the original June-6 framing but is strategically sound — it's the part John can *feel*.\n\n**Status:** Locked. Awareness revamp (which IS value-first) has shipped.\n\n#### **B. Judgment fan-out vs. serial loop**\n**Tension:** AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md §3 proposed three fan-outs: discovery (kept), serial judgment (exists at K=2), judgment parallelization (deferred). Line 128 states it is **cut until `AURORA_SWARM_TOP_K ≥ ~20`**. The decision: \"engineering theater at the current `TOP_K=2`\" — correct choice until volume justifies it.\n\n**Status:** Locked. Not a blocker.\n\n#### **C. Collection re-targeting: popularity bias risk**\n**Tension (RESEARCH.md §B-1, lines 72–73):** The ranker heuristic `frontier_score` (authority 35 / aggregator 25 / star-velocity 20 / recency 10 / bench 5 / code 5, gate ≥55) **\"structurally filters out the obscure small-author find that justifies Aurora's existence\"** — it narrows discovery toward popularity. The fix: keep a narrow raw-arxiv recall safety net, add an authority-bypass lane (strong code_linkage + benchmark_presence + recency), validate weights against John's labeled likes/rejects **before trusting any cutoff** (line 74).\n\n**Status:** PARTIALLY RESOLVED. The awareness revamp (W2) added the frontier_ranker + authority-bypass lane and runs it **shadow-only** (no production promotion) until labels accrue. Line 114 of EXECUTION-LOG.md: \"the promotion-to-cron step is documented but NOT taken.\" **This is a deliberate safety gate — correct call.**\n\n#### **D. WAL-mode SQLite diagnosis error (June 13 false alarm)**\n**Tension:** W3 escalation claimed \"migration breakage\" on the live `kb/aurora.db`. Root cause: diagnosing a WAL-mode DB by copying the `.db` file omits `-wal`, producing an inconsistent snapshot. The fix: use `mode=ro` connections or `.backup()` API for coherent snapshots.\n\n**Status:** ✅ RESOLVED. Verified 2026-06-13 by confirming the overnight sweep applied all migrations cleanly; all W2–W5 schema is live.\n\n#### **E. Adoption ground truth is n=7 (forbids automation)**\n**Tension:** The live `hh_events` table has 106 events but only n=7 carry a real decision (6 loaded, 1 dismissed). Every adoption-related signal (taste, precision, ranker weights) runs **open-loop** until n≥30. The decision (RESEARCH.md §B-2, §B-3): degrade auto-consensus \"rings\" to non-authoritative suggestions; suppress metric RATES below n<30 and show raw counts instead; explicitly name the bootstrap state in briefings.\n\n**Status:** ✅ LOCKED. Awareness revamp W5 implements this: decisions table captures labels; W4 + W5 together suppress all rates below n<30 and name the open-loop state in briefings (EXECUTION-LOG.md lines 108–112, regression test `test_rate_gates_on_terminal_decisions_not_surfaced`).\n\n#### **F. Models table was shadowed / unsurfaced**\n**Tension:** Aurora collected 352 fully-priced models (HANDOFF.md §3: \"`models` table = 352 rows, ALL priced\") but surfaced NONE of them. Meanwhile, the system spent its nightly dollar on arxiv-paper harvesting. The fix (RESEARCH.md §A, top recommendation): surface the 352-model table + an intelligence-vs-cost (price/perf) frontier + best-for-X cards immediately.\n\n**Status:** ✅ RESOLVED (W1 of awareness revamp). Dashboard now shows junk-filtered models (321/352 usable after filtering sentinels like `-1000000` and `$0` rows), price/perf frontier SVG, best-for-X cards.\n\n#### **G. Benchmark collection was zero; needs to be thin-slice**\n**Tension:** John explicitly wants \"the benches\"; `model_benchmarks` table was empty. The fix: OpenRouter `/models` (keyless, specs/pricing) + **Epoch AI CC-BY** (GPQA/SWE-bench/FrontierMath, mirror-legal) as the thin slice. With Epoch, \"which model for X, at what price/perf\" becomes answerable.\n\n**Status:** ✅ RESOLVED (W3 of awareness revamp). Migration `0027_benchmark_provenance` adds `source`+`license` to `model_benchmarks`. Epoch ingester wired. Publisher scrub blocks redistribution-restricted sources (AA, OpenRouter) from the snapshot (CC1 no-leak rule verified BOTH directions).\n\n#### **H. Delivering results through surfaces John doesn't visit vs. his morning report**\n**Tension (RESEARCH.md §B-7, lines 85–86):** \"John consumes via the report (which he called 'fine'), not by visiting pages.\" The dashboard ships with all the bells; but awareness/adoption/value surfaces must land in the **morning report or weekly email first**; dashboard is optional drill-down.\n\n**Status:** ✅ RESOLVED (W1, W4, W5 of awareness revamp). All deliverables ship report-first. EXECUTION-LOG.md W4 (lines 127–128): \"Momentum + value/health ship in the morning report AND `build_weekly_note` (CC6 report-first), not dashboard-only. Reviewers confirmed zero JSON leaks into John's rendered note.\"\n\n#### **I. Honest value framing vs. vanity metrics**\n**Tension:** Vanity metrics like \"finds/night\" or \"items collected\" obscure whether the system is actually useful. The fix: admit n<30 disqualifies rates; use (1) useful-find rate [OMTM], (2) cost per useful find, (3) precision, (4) frontier coverage, (5) decisions influenced, (6) spend-vs-budget; RAG+4-question health summary (is it working / worth it / what's wrong / what to think about?).\n\n**Status:** ✅ RESOLVED (W4 of awareness revamp). Regression tests added (`test_rate_gates_on_terminal_decisions_not_surfaced` and others) to enforce n-gating. Live briefing RAG is \"AMBER\" (structurally unreachable green while open-loop, per line 118).\n\n---\n\n### **6. KNOWLEDGE BASE ARTIFACTS & CONFIGURATION**\n\n**Key locked decisions (from NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md §17 + ongoing constraints):**\n\n| Item | Locked Value | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Runner sandbox | Docker (Docker Desktop) | §17, verified in use |\n| Scheduler | Windows Task Scheduler (primary), Cowork mirror | §17; working 01:07–06:47 real schedule |\n| Critic B | Gemini (primary), local OpenAI-compatible (fallback) | §17 |\n| Aurora root | `C:\\dev\\aurora\\` | §17 |\n| Morning briefing | 08:30 Cowork scheduled session | §17 + EXECUTION-LOG verified running |\n| API keys | Dedicated Aurora keys, $50/mo Anthropic + $10/mo Gemini caps | §17 |\n| HH threshold | 0.25 (downgraded from 0.42 and 0.65) | Wave 0 (lines 56–58) |\n| GitHub repo | `github.com/johncliechty/aurora-library` (private, personal) | §17; publisher pushes nightly tags |\n\n**Cross-cutting hard rules (from awareness revamp DESCRIPTION.md / IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md):**\n- **CC1 — Publisher no-leak:** new tables declare {scrub / publish-clean / publish-with-filter}; tested in `--dry-run`.\n- **CC2 — Live-pipeline safety:** collection changes land behind `*_shadow` / dry-run, promoted only after reviewed diff.\n- **CC3 — Honest-n:** no metric RATE shown below n<30; show raw counts + window + sample_size; name open-loop state.\n- **CC4 — KB read-only except new tables:** Never read `.env`. Never run `bin/migrate_to_kind_paper.py`'s delete step.\n- **CC5 — Provenance at write time:** Benchmark/model cells carry NOT-NULL `source` + `license` + `observed_at` + contamination flags.\n- **CC6 — Report-first delivery:** Each wave ships value in morning-report / weekly-email first; dashboard is optional.\n- **CC7 — Reuse, don't rebuild:** Evolve existing `dashboard/` + `kb/aurora.db` schema (additive migrations only).\n\n---\n\