as the cron.\n\n**Friction John flagged (HANDOFF.md §2):**\n| # | Reaction | Real ask |\n|---|---|---|\n| B | \"Nothing new last night but we still spent money.\" | **Honest value accounting:** what did the spend buy? Is it finding things worth the money? |\n| C | Suggested adoption — is this something I act on? | Make adoption **actionable**: a review tab with human-readable summary, risks, advantages, **why adopt / why not**. |\n| D | **Health page: \"completely not helpful… looks like something a computer might read.\"** | **Human-readable health + value:** plain-English \"is it working, is it worth it, what's wrong, what should I think about.\" |\n| E | What was new — wants it **by category** + **models + pricing** + \"am I actually collecting anything?\" | A **category intelligence** surface: per-category \"what's the current best-in-class + what's newly notable,\" not a raw nightly dump. |\n| F | Catalog map: not interested. Wants a **knowledge / relationship map**. | A **human-readable relationship map** of the agentic-AI landscape — how systems relate — not a taxonomy. |\n\n**The existential complaint (RESEARCH.md §C, lines 93–95):**\n> \"Stripped of framing, a night delivers 8-21 arxiv papers + ~20 rejections to a polished read-only dashboard; last night produced **zero** skills/tools/agents. The system built to track harnesses/models/benchmarks/skills spent its dollar on the one category John mentioned in passing.\"\n\n**Value asymmetry (RESEARCH.md §B-3, lines 75–77):**\n> \"Live `hh_events`: 106 events but only **n=7 carry a decision** (6 loaded, 1 dismissed) across 21 queries / 10 sessions / 3 weeks... show raw counts; the plan must explicitly name that until usage exists, every learned/derived signal (taste, precision, ring) runs **open-loop**.\"\n\n---\n\n### **5. EXPLICIT TENSIONS & UNRESOLVED DECISIONS**\n\n#### **A. Architecture vs. Value — Co-equal or Sequential?**\n**Tension:** AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md (June 6) locked \"felt, trustworthy value *and*