{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D3vS1XSt6PQR86K5UNE1p5","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have enough context. Let me compile a rigorous evidence-based report on Aurora's actual value delivery.\n\n---\n\n## RIGOROUS INVESTIGATION: AURORA'S VALUE DELIVERY\n\nBased on deep examination of the codebase, execution logs, and live metrics, here is an evidence-based assessment of whether Aurora delivers value.\n\n### 1. DISCOVERY QUALITY — The Foreman Handoff Evidence\n\n**What was locked as the North Star:**  \n\"Everything Aurora surfaces to John is correctly classified, genuinely interesting, and worth his attention — a smaller, high-trust catalog with a closed, measurable value loop.\"\n\n**Evidence from Wave 1–5 Execution (EXECUTION-LOG.md):**\n\n- **Wave 1 (June 10):** \"top_finds = 5 named eligible badged skills, zero raw IDs / local: / vendor / paper / model\" — the briefing is delivering **named, ranked artifacts with why-lines**. This is working.\n- **Wave 2 (June 10):** \"Simulated post-apply noise_audit: all categories 0\" (arxiv_as_tool_agent 0, vendor_tools 0, pointer_artifacts 0). The **ingest gate is clean**.\n- **Wave 3 (June 10):** \"Stargazer coverage = 100% (249/249 active GitHub-linked)\" — link health probes work, 8 papers delivered in the first real digest.\n- **Wave 4 (June 10):** \"30 cost rows, $0.0446 metered... interest_score range 0.16–0.78, interest_why profile-aligned\" — the taste scorer is **live and priced correctly** (E17: tag identity verified).\n- **Wave 5 (June 10):** \"stale_candidates 7→0, cold_candidates 0, local skills 822-824 protected — nothing retires tonight\" — the retirement safety gate **prevented 7 live artifacts from being deleted** in same-day duplicate probes.\n\n**The \"dirty tree IS production\" trap was flagged and validated:**  \n`\"the working tree IS production (sweeps 01:07–05:03, briefing 06:47): every wave ends with a clean committed tree\"` — this constraint is real and enforced.\n\n**Critical issue FOUND: key traps were avoided by design**\n- The `migrate_to_kind_paper.py` delete step that could have deleted 3 local skills (822-824) is **permanently dead code** per the spec.\n- The orphan-card and cross-kind retire sweeps **prevent library filesystem corruption**.\n\n**Verdict:** Discovery quality is HIGH for what it covers. The catalog is **correctly classified** (no arxiv slipping through as tools), **curated** (noise audit = 0), and **ranked** (taste + stars + evidence badges). **However**, see the collection skew below.\n\n---\n\n### 2. LIBRARY OUTPUT — Quality of Curated Entries\n\n**Sample entries examined:**\n\nFrom `library/agents/ask-user/index.md`:\n```\n**What problem it solves**\n- **Domain (axis 1):** `agent-internals > tool-use`\n- **Complexity (axis 2):** rank 1 (recipe)\n\n_Embedder rationale: Reusable pattern for human-in-the-loop decision gating..._\n\n## Validation history\n| Date | Stage | Verdict | Score | Notes |\n| 2026-06-23 | static | pass | 0.85 | Front-matter parsed via front_matter_strict...\n```\n\nFrom `library/agents/capture/index.md` — identical structure with domain/complexity analysis.\n\nFrom `library/models/ai21/jamba-large-1-7-latest/index.md`:\n```\n**Capacity profile**\n| Field | Value |\n| Context (in) | 256K |\n| Max output | 4K |\n| Modalities | text |\n| Tool use | unknown |\n| Price $/1M in | $2 |\n| Price $/1M out | $8 |\n| Benchmarks | _No benchmark rows this cycle_ |\n```\n\n**What changed across all ~80 library entries (git diff stats):**\n- Agent/tool/skill entries: 6–10 line changes (metadata/timestamp updates).\n- Model entries: 4-line changes (simple field updates).\n- The `library/models/_grid.md` saw 61 changed lines (content regeneration).\n\n**Signal:** Mass changes across library/ suggest **a templating or format change on 2026-06-23** — the entries are being **regenerated or reformatted in bulk** rather than individually updated. The library entries are **thin scaffolds** (front-matter parsed, complexity ranked, but validation is \"static\" only, and \"Swarm validation not yet run — P3 will add runner\").\n\n**Key quote from the entries:**  \n\"(Boilerplate fallback — no reconciler verdict yet. Static-only path; swarm validation will replace this on the next sweep.)\"\n\n**Verdict:** Library entries are **HIGH-QUALITY STRUCTURED DATA** (taxonomy, domain/complexity, priced models) but **LIGHTWEIGHT ON NARRATIVE** (why it matters, how to use it) and **MISSING HUMAN VALIDATION** (swarm validation \"P3 will add\"). The entries are **decision-ready scaffolds, not curated essays**. Usable for machines (Helping Hand embedding, YAML parsing), **thin for human navigation**.\n\n---\n\n### 3. HELPING HAND — The Recommender Mechanics\n\n**How matching works:**\n- **Recall:** Gemini-embedding-2 (semantic, live) OR keyword-overlap fallback\n- **Gating:** Gemini 3.5 Flash \"MoE router\" (Mixture of Experts judge) picks the single best match or null\n- **Score gate:** `HELPING_HAND_THRESHOLD_DEFAULT = 0.25` (hard-coded, sourced from \"7 historical terminal events at scores [0.19, 0.25, 0.31, 0.33, 0.55, 0.64]\")\n- **Repetition gate:** If last 3 turns > 0.7 similarity, suppress auto-load (tight-loop prevention)\n\n**The \"GWL v0.1 Protocol\" (from CLAUDE.md):**\n```json\n{\n  \"query\": \"...\",\n  \"agent_context\": {\n    \"calling_agent\": \"expert-coder\",\n    \"project_type\": \"finance\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\"GWL v0.1 Protocol (Recursive Calls)\" — this is **named but marked aspirational** (\"the skill encodes the calling protocol\"). **No evidence this is used yet** (the protocol is documented, not implemented).\n\n**Usage feedback (log_use):**\nThe `log_use` endpoint exists in server.py and writes to `hh_events` table. But:\n\nFrom `latest_summary.json`:\n```json\n\"useful_find_rate\": {\n  \"status\": \"open_loop\",\n  \"rate\": null,\n  \"sample_size\": 7,\n  \"detail\": \"Useful-find rate: 6 loaded of 98 surfaced (7 decided)\"\n}\n```\n\nOnly **7 decisions logged all-time**, with 0 logged this week. The system explicitly states:\n> \"Too early to say — only 7 decision(s) logged so far, below the 30 needed to trust a rate.\"\n\n**The score gate is documented but doesn't prevent low-signal matches:**\nThe 0.25 floor stops MoE from running on very weak candidates, but all 98 surfaced matches still get recorded in `hh_events` with outcome='surfaced'. The gate is **soft** (MoE doesn't run) not **hard** (match isn't shown).\n\n**Verdict:** Helping Hand is **WELL-ENGINEERED ARCHITECTURE** (embedding-fallback resilience, repetition-gate safety, time-decay on usage feedback) but **USAGE SIGNALS ARE ANEMIC** (7 logged decisions vs 30 needed to validate). The system is **set up correctly but not being used** — or John is deferring judgment until the catalog reaches scale.\n\n---\n\n### 4. COST AUDIT — What Aurora Costs to Run\n\n**From pricing.yaml:**\n\nModel spend (nightly sweeps use):\n- **Scout:** Gemini-3.5-flash (estimated, unverified, $0)\n- **Runner/Critics/Librarian:** Sonnet 4.6 ($3/$15) or Gemini 3.5 Flash ($0)\n- **Taste scorer:** Claude Haiku 4.5 ($1/$5) — Wave 4, 30 calls/night → $0.0446 metered live\n\n**Monthly cost (from latest_summary.json, as of 2026-06-23):**\n```json\n\"costs\": {\n  \"anthropic_mtd\": 22.034652,\n  \"gemini_mtd\": 0.0022862\n},\n\"spend_vs_budget\": {\n  \"rate\": 0.44069304,  // 44% of budget\n  \"detail\": \"Spend (MTD): anthropic $22.03/$50 · gemini $0.00/$10\"\n}\n```\n\n**Cost-per-find (from the latest briefing):**\n> \"Can't honestly price it yet — $33.02 spent over 6 useful find(s) — open-loop (n=6, need >=30 to trust a per-find cost).\"\n\n**Nightly sweep schedule:**\n- 01:07, 02:19, 03:41, 05:03 (skills/tools/agents sweeps)\n- 06:47 (briefing delivery)\n\n**Evidence of cost awareness:**\n- The PRICING_GUARDRAILS.md doc (2026-05-25) explicitly flags the **Opus 4.6 hallucination incident** where an LLM falsely claimed $15/$75 pricing, and the guardrails prevent that from corrupting `kb/pricing.yaml`.\n- The `verify_citation()` gate requires deterministic web fetch + regex — \"no LLM in this path.\"\n- The taste scorer is **provably metered** (E17 verified: resp.model == called tag == priced tag).\n\n**Verdict:** Cost is **$22 MTD on $50 Anthropic budget + $0 on $10 Gemini** (44% spend). Per-find cost is **$5.50 / useful find** (provisional, n=6). The system is **self-aware about cost** (metering is tight, not estimated), but **value ROI is unmeasured** due to low usage.\n\n---\n\n### 5. THE FUNDAMENTAL VALUE QUESTION — Write-Only Archive vs. Decision Driver?\n\n**Evidence Aurora is being CONSULTED:**\n\nFrom latest_summary.json:\n```json\n\"productivity_index\": 0.23809523809523808,  // 24% adoption, n=21 queries ever\n\"session_note\": \"written\",\n\"delivery\": {\n  \"toast\": \"error\"  // briefing toast delivery is FAILING\n}\n```\n\nThe **briefing is generated daily** (06:47, delivered to `reports/morning/latest_briefing_note.md`), but:\n- **No evidence of reading.** The delivery log shows \"toast: error\" — the toast notification to John is NOT working.\n- **Usage is near-zero.** 7 decisions logged all-time (most from the initial seeding).\n- **Weekly digest shows 0 adoption this week:** From 2026-06-14 digest: \"Suggestion adoption this week: 0% (flat vs 0%)\" and \"Loads / dismissals this week: 0 loaded · 0 dismissed\"\n\n**The handoff doc (HANDOFF.md, 2026-06-11) flagged this directly:**\n\nFrom John's live feedback:\n> \"Nothing new last night but we still spent money.\"\n\nAnd later:\n> \"Is this something I act on?\" — Make adoption actionable: a tab to review candidate adoptions, each with a human-readable summary, risks, advantages, why adopt / why not, and an accept/decline.\n\nThe handoff **explicitly names the value gap:**\n> \"Aurora today is a **discovery+hygiene pipeline with an ops dashboard**. John wants an **agentic-AI awareness+decision instrument**.\"\n\n**Further evidence of write-only smell:**\n\nFrom the aurora-awareness-revamp research brief:\n> \"The models goldmine is collected but unsurfaced. `models` table = 352 rows, ALL priced... BUT data quality is mixed... coverage capped at 65%.\"\n\n> \"The $/night largely buys arxiv-paper harvesting + screening, not the harnesses/models/skills John cares about.\"\n\n> \"About benchmarks: `model_benchmarks` = 0 rows. John explicitly wants 'the benches.' This is a collection gap, not just a surface gap.\"\n\n**Metric showing non-adoption:**\n\nFrom the weekly digests I examined:\n- 2026-06-14: \"Suggestion adoption this week: 0%\" (shown explicitly)\n- 2026-06-21: No adoption metrics shown (implicit zero)\n\n**Verdict:** Aurora is **generating high-quality output but not reaching John as decision-driving input.** The briefing toast is broken (\"toast: error\"), adoption is near-zero (7 decisions all-time), and John himself flagged that the surface doesn't drive action. **The catalog is real and well-curated, but the feedback loop is open — discoveries are recorded but not consulted.**\n\n---\n\n### 6. BENCHMARK / DECISION-GRADE MODEL VIEW\n\n**W3 awareness revamp benchmark (thin-slice):**\n\nThe `W3` phase was supposed to run a link-health probe on GitHub artifacts to surface stars as a \"quality signal.\" From the EXECUTION-LOG:\n> \"stargazer coverage = 100% (249/249 active GitHub-linked)\"\n\n**But benchmarks themselves are zero:**\n\nFrom the latest_summary.json:\n```json\n\"models\": {\n  \"benchmarks\": null\n}\n```\n\nFrom the research handoff:\n> \"`model_benchmarks` = **0 rows**. John explicitly wants 'the benches.' This is a collection gap, not just a surface gap.\"\n\n**What exists vs. what's missing:**\n\nExists:\n- 352 priced models (price_in, price_out, context, modalities, tool_use, reasoning_mode, knowledge_cutoff, license_class, released, deprecation)\n- GitHub stars (link_health.gh_stargazers for 249 artifacts)\n\nMissing:\n- Model benchmarks (0 rows)\n- \"Best-in-class\" ranking (the awareness revamp says this requires \"ranking + junk filtering + a 'best-in-class' notion\")\n- Benchmark data collection (not in the current sweep pipeline)\n\n**Verdict:** The benchmark/model-awareness view is **aspirational, not real.** Stars are collected but not presented. Model pricing is accurate and metered, but bench marks don't exist, and the \"best-in-class models + pricing\" view John requested is **planned but not delivered**.\n\n---\n\n### SUMMARY — VALUE DELIVERY SCORECARD\n\n| Dimension | Evidence | Grade |\n|-----------|----------|-------|\n| **Discovery Quality** | Noise audit = 0, taxonomy correct, taste scorer live, 5-wave de-noising completed | ✅ A |\n| **Catalog Curation** | 307 artifacts, structured metadata, confidence badges, domain/complexity ranking | ✅ A- |\n| **Library UX** | Scaffolding complete, swarm validation pending, entries thin on narrative | 🟡 B |\n| **Helping Hand Architecture** | Embedding+fallback, MoE judge, repetition gate, usage modifier bounded, safety-proofed | ✅ A |\n| **Helping Hand Usage** | 7 decisions logged all-time, 0 this week, adoption index 24% (n=21 all-time) | 🔴 F |\n| **Cost Awareness** | Metering tight, guardrails verified, price corruption incident prevented | ✅ A |\n| **Cost Value** | $22 MTD on $50 budget, $5.50 per useful find (n=6, provisional) | 🟡 B- |\n| **Briefing Delivery** | Daily generation, top-finds + health summary well-written, toast notification BROKEN | 🟡 B |\n| **Decision-Driving Impact** | Briefing read?=unknown, suggestions acted on?=no (n=0 logged this week) | 🔴 F |\n| **Model Benchmarks** | 352 priced models collected, 0 benchmarks, ranking missing, unsurfaced | 🔴 F |\n\n---\n\n## THE CORE FINDING\n\n**Aurora generates excellent output (high-quality discovery, clean catalog, verified cost metering) but does not drive John's decisions.**\n\nThe system is **optimized for collection quality and pipeline hygiene**, not for **actionability and impact**. Specific gaps:\n\n1. **The briefing is siloed.** Toast delivery is broken; John reads a Markdown file, but there's no signal that it drives action. (0 adoptions logged this week.)\n\n2. **Suggestions are passive.** Helping Hand surfaces matches, but there's no **adoption review queue** where John can see \"risks, advantages, why adopt / why not, and accept/decline\" — the gap John explicitly named in his 2026-06-11 feedback.\n\n3. **Model / benchmark awareness is missing.** 352 models are priced and stored but not surfaced. Benchmarks (0 rows) are not collected at all.\n\n4. **Collection skew:** The sweeps harvest ~15–21 papers/night but produce 0–1 skills/tools/agents/day. The cost largely buys arxiv ingestion, not the harnesses/skills John cares about.\n\n5. **The value loop is open.** Usage feedback (log_use) exists but is near-zero (7 events all-time). The system cannot optimize what it doesn't observe.\n\n**What Aurora *does* deliver:** A **trustworthy, well-curated, correctly-classified catalog** of the agentic-AI ecosystem, with **tight cost controls and safety-proofed automation**. It is **production-grade infrastructure** for a *discovery system*, not yet a *decision-support system*.\n\nThe 2026-06-11 handoff to researchPrime+Crucible correctly identified the delta. Aurora is not broken — it is incomplete. It needs the **adoption queue, human-readable value framing, benchmarks, and decision feedback** that John's reactions highlighted."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e9f13f6-4032-41a4-8d9f-b9e18c221609","uuid":"bc1f0b7b-f713-4eab-b5ad-794691bc7a73","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:41:37.518Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are exploring the Aurora project at C:\\dev\\aurora to support a deep-think advisory review. I need a rigorous, evidence-based picture of whether Aurora actually delivers VALUE — the quality of what it discovers and how that value reaches the user.\n\nInvestigate and report:\n1. Discovery quality: read C:\\dev\\aurora\\docs\\foreman-handoff-quality\\ (all waves) and any \"discovery-quality\" docs. What problem was being solved? What were the \"key traps\" (dirty tree IS production, real schedule 01:07-06:47, never run migrate_to_kind_paper delete step)? Is discovery producing real, validated, useful artifacts or noise?\n2. The library/ output: sample a handful of library/agents/*/index.md and library/models/*/index.md entries. Are these high-quality curated entries, or thin auto-generated scaffolds? Quote examples. The git status shows ~all of library/ is modified — what changed across all of them at once (a templating/format change)? That's a signal — investigate what mass-rewrites the whole library.\n3. Helping Hand: the recommender (helping-hand-plugin/, mcp-servers/aurora-kb/). How does it surface matches? What is the score gate (0.65)? Does it actually get used — any usage logs (log_use)? Is the \"GWL v0.1 Protocol\" real or aspirational?\n4. Cost: any cost-audit docs (docs mentioning cost-audit-2026-06-05). What does Aurora cost to run nightly/monthly? Is the value worth the spend for a single user?\n5. The fundamental question: this is a single-user system that John runs to catalog the Claude/agent ecosystem. Look for evidence of whether the catalog is actually CONSULTED and drives decisions, vs. being a write-only archive that's generated but never read. Any analytics, access logs, \"log_use\" entries, or evidence of the library being queried?\n6. Benchmark / \"decision-grade model view\" (W3 awareness revamp benchmark thin-slice) — what does it actually benchmark and is the data real?\n\nGive verbatim quotes/snippets with file paths. Be skeptical: distinguish \"generates a lot of output\" from \"produces consulted, decision-driving value.\" Flag write-only-archive smell, vanity metrics, and any gap between effort spent and value realized.","agentId":"ac85f5ec85a4c63c2","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have enough context. Let me compile a rigorous evidence-based report on Aurora's actual value delivery.\n\n---\n\n## RIGOROUS INVESTIGATION: AURORA'S VALUE DELIVERY\n\nBased on deep examination of the codebase, execution logs, and live metrics, here is an evidence-based assessment of whether Aurora delivers value.\n\n### 1. DISCOVERY QUALITY — The Foreman Handoff Evidence\n\n**What was locked as the North Star:**  \n\"Everything Aurora surfaces to John is correctly classified, genuinely interesting, and worth his attention — a smaller, high-trust catalog with a closed, measurable value loop.\"\n\n**Evidence from Wave 1–5 Execution (EXECUTION-LOG.md):**\n\n- **Wave 1 (June 10):** \"top_finds = 5 named eligible badged skills, zero raw IDs / local: / vendor / paper / model\" — the briefing is delivering **named, ranked artifacts with why-lines**. This is working.\n- **Wave 2 (June 10):** \"Simulated post-apply noise_audit: all categories 0\" (arxiv_as_tool_agent 0, vendor_tools 0, pointer_artifacts 0). The **ingest gate is clean**.\n- **Wave 3 (June 10):** \"Stargazer coverage = 100% (249/249 active GitHub-linked)\" — link health probes work, 8 papers delivered in the first real digest.\n- **Wave 4 (June 10):** \"30 cost rows, $0.0446 metered... interest_score range 0.16–0.78, interest_why profile-aligned\" — the taste scorer is **live and priced correctly** (E17: tag identity verified).\n- **Wave 5 (June 10):** \"stale_candidates 7→0, cold_candidates 0, local skills 822-824 protected — nothing retires tonight\" — the retirement safety gate **prevented 7 live artifacts from being deleted** in same-day duplicate probes.\n\n**The \"dirty tree IS production\" trap was flagged and validated:**  \n`\"the working tree IS production (sweeps 01:07–05:03, briefing 06:47): every wave ends with a clean committed tree\"` — this constraint is real and enforced.\n\n**Critical issue FOUND: key traps were avoided by design**\n- The `migrate_to_kind_paper.py` delete step that could have deleted 3 local skills (822-824) is **permanently dead code** per the spec.\n- The orphan-card and cross-kind retire sweeps **prevent library filesystem corruption**.\n\n**Verdict:** Discovery quality is HIGH for what it covers. The catalog is **correctly classified** (no arxiv slipping through as tools), **curated** (noise audit = 0), and **ranked** (taste + stars + evidence badges). **However**, see the collection skew below.\n\n---\n\n### 2. LIBRARY OUTPUT — Quality of Curated Entries\n\n**Sample entries examined:**\n\nFrom `library/agents/ask-user/index.md`:\n```\n**What problem it solves**\n- **Domain (axis 1):** `agent-internals > tool-use`\n- **Complexity (axis 2):** rank 1 (recipe)\n\n_Embedder rationale: Reusable pattern for human-in-the-loop decision gating..._\n\n## Validation history\n| Date | Stage | Verdict | Score | Notes |\n| 2026-06-23 | static | pass | 0.85 | Front-matter parsed via front_matter_strict...\n```\n\nFrom `library/agents/capture/index.md` — identical structure with domain/complexity analysis.\n\nFrom `library/models/ai21/jamba-large-1-7-latest/index.md`:\n```\n**Capacity profile**\n| Field | Value |\n| Context (in) | 256K |\n| Max output | 4K |\n| Modalities | text |\n| Tool use | unknown |\n| Price $/1M in | $2 |\n| Price $/1M out | $8 |\n| Benchmarks | _No benchmark rows this cycle_ |\n```\n\n**What changed across all ~80 library entries (git diff stats):**\n- Agent/tool/skill entries: 6–10 line changes (metadata/timestamp updates).\n- Model entries: 4-line changes (simple field updates).\n- The `library/models/_grid.md` saw 61 changed lines (content regeneration).\n\n**Signal:** Mass changes across library/ suggest **a templating or format change on 2026-06-23** — the entries are being **regenerated or reformatted in bulk** rather than individually updated. The library entries are **thin scaffolds** (front-matter parsed, complexity ranked, but validation is \"static\" only, and \"Swarm validation not yet run — P3 will add runner\").\n\n**Key quote from the entries:**  \n\"(Boilerplate fallback — no reconciler verdict yet. Static-only path; swarm validation will replace this on the next sweep.)\"\n\n**Verdict:** Library entries are **HIGH-QUALITY STRUCTURED DATA** (taxonomy, domain/complexity, priced models) but **LIGHTWEIGHT ON NARRATIVE** (why it matters, how to use it) and **MISSING HUMAN VALIDATION** (swarm validation \"P3 will add\"). The entries are **decision-ready scaffolds, not curated essays**. Usable for machines (Helping Hand embedding, YAML parsing), **thin for human navigation**.\n\n---\n\n### 3. HELPING HAND — The Recommender Mechanics\n\n**How matching works:**\n- **Recall:** Gemini-embedding-2 (semantic, live) OR keyword-overlap fallback\n- **Gating:** Gemini 3.5 Flash \"MoE router\" (Mixture of Experts judge) picks the single best match or null\n- **Score gate:** `HELPING_HAND_THRESHOLD_DEFAULT = 0.25` (hard-coded, sourced from \"7 historical terminal events at scores [0.19, 0.25, 0.31, 0.33, 0.55, 0.64]\")\n- **Repetition gate:** If last 3 turns > 0.7 similarity, suppress auto-load (tight-loop prevention)\n\n**The \"GWL v0.1 Protocol\" (from CLAUDE.md):**\n```json\n{\n  \"query\": \"...\",\n  \"agent_context\": {\n    \"calling_agent\": \"expert-coder\",\n    \"project_type\": \"finance\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\"GWL v0.1 Protocol (Recursive Calls)\" — this is **named but marked aspirational** (\"the skill encodes the calling protocol\"). **No evidence this is used yet** (the protocol is documented, not implemented).\n\n**Usage feedback (log_use):**\nThe `log_use` endpoint exists in server.py and writes to `hh_events` table. But:\n\nFrom `latest_summary.json`:\n```json\n\"useful_find_rate\": {\n  \"status\": \"open_loop\",\n  \"rate\": null,\n  \"sample_size\": 7,\n  \"detail\": \"Useful-find rate: 6 loaded of 98 surfaced (7 decided)\"\n}\n```\n\nOnly **7 decisions logged all-time**, with 0 logged this week. The system explicitly states:\n> \"Too early to say — only 7 decision(s) logged so far, below the 30 needed to trust a rate.\"\n\n**The score gate is documented but doesn't prevent low-signal matches:**\nThe 0.25 floor stops MoE from running on very weak candidates, but all 98 surfaced matches still get recorded in `hh_events` with outcome='surfaced'. The gate is **soft** (MoE doesn't run) not **hard** (match isn't shown).\n\n**Verdict:** Helping Hand is **WELL-ENGINEERED ARCHITECTURE** (embedding-fallback resilience, repetition-gate safety, time-decay on usage feedback) but **USAGE SIGNALS ARE ANEMIC** (7 logged decisions vs 30 needed to validate). The system is **set up correctly but not being used** — or John is deferring judgment until the catalog reaches scale.\n\n---\n\n### 4. COST AUDIT — What Aurora Costs to Run\n\n**From pricing.yaml:**\n\nModel spend (nightly sweeps use):\n- **Scout:** Gemini-3.5-flash (estimated, unverified, $0)\n- **Runner/Critics/Librarian:** Sonnet 4.6 ($3/$15) or Gemini 3.5 Flash ($0)\n- **Taste scorer:** Claude Haiku 4.5 ($1/$5) — Wave 4, 30 calls/night → $0.0446 metered live\n\n**Monthly cost (from latest_summary.json, as of 2026-06-23):**\n```json\n\"costs\": {\n  \"anthropic_mtd\": 22.034652,\n  \"gemini_mtd\": 0.0022862\n},\n\"spend_vs_budget\": {\n  \"rate\": 0.44069304,  // 44% of budget\n  \"detail\": \"Spend (MTD): anthropic $22.03/$50 · gemini $0.00/$10\"\n}\n```\n\n**Cost-per-find (from the latest briefing):**\n> \"Can't honestly price it yet — $33.02 spent over 6 useful find(s) — open-loop (n=6, need >=30 to trust a per-find cost).\"\n\n**Nightly sweep schedule:**\n- 01:07, 02:19, 03:41, 05:03 (skills/tools/agents sweeps)\n- 06:47 (briefing delivery)\n\n**Evidence of cost awareness:**\n- The PRICING_GUARDRAILS.md doc (2026-05-25) explicitly flags the **Opus 4.6 hallucination incident** where an LLM falsely claimed $15/$75 pricing, and the guardrails prevent that from corrupting `kb/pricing.yaml`.\n- The `verify_citation()` gate requires deterministic web fetch + regex — \"no LLM in this path.\"\n- The taste scorer is **provably metered** (E17 verified: resp.model == called tag == priced tag).\n\n**Verdict:** Cost is **$22 MTD on $50 Anthropic budget + $0 on $10 Gemini** (44% spend). Per-find cost is **$5.50 / useful find** (provisional, n=6). The system is **self-aware about cost** (metering is tight, not estimated), but **value ROI is unmeasured** due to low usage.\n\n---\n\n### 5. THE FUNDAMENTAL VALUE QUESTION — Write-Only Archive vs. Decision Driver?\n\n**Evidence Aurora is being CONSULTED:**\n\nFrom latest_summary.json:\n```json\n\"productivity_index\": 0.23809523809523808,  // 24% adoption, n=21 queries ever\n\"session_note\": \"written\",\n\"delivery\": {\n  \"toast\": \"error\"  // briefing toast delivery is FAILING\n}\n```\n\nThe **briefing is generated daily** (06:47, delivered to `reports/morning/latest_briefing_note.md`), but:\n- **No evidence of reading.** The delivery log shows \"toast: error\" — the toast notification to John is NOT working.\n- **Usage is near-zero.** 7 decisions logged all-time (most from the initial seeding).\n- **Weekly digest shows 0 adoption this week:** From 2026-06-14 digest: \"Suggestion adoption this week: 0% (flat vs 0%)\" and \"Loads / dismissals this week: 0 loaded · 0 dismissed\"\n\n**The handoff doc (HANDOFF.md, 2026-06-11) flagged this directly:**\n\nFrom John's live feedback:\n> \"Nothing new last night but we still spent money.\"\n\nAnd later:\n> \"Is this something I act on?\" — Make adoption actionable: a tab to review candidate adoptions, each with a human-readable summary, risks, advantages, why adopt / why not, and an accept/decline.\n\nThe handoff **explicitly names the value gap:**\n> \"Aurora today is a **discovery+hygiene pipeline with an ops dashboard**. John wants an **agentic-AI awareness+decision instrument**.\"\n\n**Further evidence of write-only smell:**\n\nFrom the aurora-awareness-revamp research brief:\n> \"The models goldmine is collected but unsurfaced. `models` table = 352 rows, ALL priced... BUT data quality is mixed... coverage capped at 65%.\"\n\n> \"The $/night largely buys arxiv-paper harvesting + screening, not the harnesses/models/skills John cares about.\"\n\n> \"About benchmarks: `model_benchmarks` = 0 rows. John explicitly wants 'the benches.' This is a collection gap, not just a surface gap.\"\n\n**Metric showing non-adoption:**\n\nFrom the weekly digests I examined:\n- 2026-06-14: \"Suggestion adoption this week: 0%\" (shown explicitly)\n- 2026-06-21: No adoption metrics shown (implicit zero)\n\n**Verdict:** Aurora is **generating high-quality output but not reaching John as decision-driving input.** The briefing toast is broken (\"toast: error\"), adoption is near-zero (7 decisions all-time), and John himself flagged that the surface doesn't drive action. **The catalog is real and well-curated, but the feedback loop is open — discoveries are recorded but not consulted.**\n\n---\n\n### 6. BENCHMARK / DECISION-GRADE MODEL VIEW\n\n**W3 awareness revamp benchmark (thin-slice):**\n\nThe `W3` phase was supposed to run a link-health probe on GitHub artifacts to surface stars as a \"quality signal.\" From the EXECUTION-LOG:\n> \"stargazer coverage = 100% (249/249 active GitHub-linked)\"\n\n**But benchmarks themselves are zero:**\n\nFrom the latest_summary.json:\n```json\n\"models\": {\n  \"benchmarks\": null\n}\n```\n\nFrom the research handoff:\n> \"`model_benchmarks` = **0 rows**. John explicitly wants 'the benches.' This is a collection gap, not just a surface gap.\"\n\n**What exists vs. what's missing:**\n\nExists:\n- 352 priced models (price_in, price_out, context, modalities, tool_use, reasoning_mode, knowledge_cutoff, license_class, released, deprecation)\n- GitHub stars (link_health.gh_stargazers for 249 artifacts)\n\nMissing:\n- Model benchmarks (0 rows)\n- \"Best-in-class\" ranking (the awareness revamp says this requires \"ranking + junk filtering + a 'best-in-class' notion\")\n- Benchmark data collection (not in the current sweep pipeline)\n\n**Verdict:** The benchmark/model-awareness view is **aspirational, not real.** Stars are collected but not presented. Model pricing is accurate and metered, but bench marks don't exist, and the \"best-in-class models + pricing\" view John requested is **planned but not delivered**.\n\n---\n\n### SUMMARY — VALUE DELIVERY SCORECARD\n\n| Dimension | Evidence | Grade |\n|-----------|----------|-------|\n| **Discovery Quality** | Noise audit = 0, taxonomy correct, taste scorer live, 5-wave de-noising completed | ✅ A |\n| **Catalog Curation** | 307 artifacts, structured metadata, confidence badges, domain/complexity ranking | ✅ A- |\n| **Library UX** | Scaffolding complete, swarm validation pending, entries thin on narrative | 🟡 B |\n| **Helping Hand Architecture** | Embedding+fallback, MoE judge, repetition gate, usage modifier bounded, safety-proofed | ✅ A |\n| **Helping Hand Usage** | 7 decisions logged all-time, 0 this week, adoption index 24% (n=21 all-time) | 🔴 F |\n| **Cost Awareness** | Metering tight, guardrails verified, price corruption incident prevented | ✅ A |\n| **Cost Value** | $22 MTD on $50 budget, $5.50 per useful find (n=6, provisional) | 🟡 B- |\n| **Briefing Delivery** | Daily generation, top-finds + health summary well-written, toast notification BROKEN | 🟡 B |\n| **Decision-Driving Impact** | Briefing read?=unknown, suggestions acted on?=no (n=0 logged this week) | 🔴 F |\n| **Model Benchmarks** | 352 priced models collected, 0 benchmarks, ranking missing, unsurfaced | 🔴 F |\n\n---\n\n## THE CORE FINDING\n\n**Aurora generates excellent output (high-quality discovery, clean catalog, verified cost metering) but does not drive John's decisions.**\n\nThe system is **optimized for collection quality and pipeline hygiene**, not for **actionability and impact**. Specific gaps:\n\n1. **The briefing is siloed.** Toast delivery is broken; John reads a Markdown file, but there's no signal that it drives action. (0 adoptions logged this week.)\n\n2. **Suggestions are passive.** Helping Hand surfaces matches, but there's no **adoption review queue** where John can see \"risks, advantages, why adopt / why not, and accept/decline\" — the gap John explicitly named in his 2026-06-11 feedback.\n\n3. **Model / benchmark awareness is missing.** 352 models are priced and stored but not surfaced. Benchmarks (0 rows) are not collected at all.\n\n4. **Collection skew:** The sweeps harvest ~15–21 papers/night but produce 0–1 skills/tools/agents/day. The cost largely buys arxiv ingestion, not the harnesses/skills John cares about.\n\n5. **The value loop is open.** Usage feedback (log_use) exists but is near-zero (7 events all-time). The system cannot optimize what it doesn't observe.\n\n**What Aurora *does* deliver:** A **trustworthy, well-curated, correctly-classified catalog** of the agentic-AI ecosystem, with **tight cost controls and safety-proofed automation**. It is **production-grade infrastructure** for a *discovery system*, not yet a *decision-support system*.\n\nThe 2026-06-11 handoff to researchPrime+Crucible correctly identified the delta. Aurora is not broken — it is incomplete. It needs the **adoption queue, human-readable value framing, benchmarks, and decision feedback** that John's reactions highlighted."}],"resolvedModel":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","totalDurationMs":111634,"totalTokens":81890,"totalToolUseCount":43,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5140,"cache_read_input_tokens":72297,"output_tokens":4448,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5140},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":5,"output_tokens":4448,"cache_read_input_tokens":72297,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5140,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5140,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":20,"searchCount":12,"bashCount":11,"editFileCount":0,"