spent > cap, break early\n- Budget-exceeded flag written to DB, read post-sweep to stamp run as 'partial' (lines 177-189, 1425-1432)\n\n**Summary of flow (walk_pipeline, orchestrator.py:614-1028):**\n```\n[1] seed_map loaded\n[2] scout (async fan-out)\n[3] quarantine wrap\n[3.5] sanitizer (cheap injection scrub, optional)\n[4] static_screener → survivors\n[5] split into swarm-top-K (default 2) + static-only tail\n[6] swarm loop: runner→critic_a+critic_b+critic_c→reconciler→evidence→embedder→librarian\n[7] static loop: embedder→librarian (no swarm)\n[8] cost rollup + exec summary write\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. LLM.PY — MODEL DEFINITIONS & CACHING/BATCHING/STRUCTURED OUTPUT\n\n**Model IDs in use (llm.py:319-320, orchestrator.py:557-564):**\n\n| Role | Vendor | Default Model | Fallback |\n|------|--------|---------------|----------|\n| runner | anthropic | claude-sonnet-4-6 | claude-haiku-4-5-20251001 (on retry exhaustion) |\n| critic_a | anthropic | claude-sonnet-4-6 | (same fallback) |\n| critic_b | gemini | gemini-3.5-flash | claude-haiku (on gemini failure + AURORA_DISABLE_GEMINI) |\n| critic_c | deepseek/groq | varies | optional (abstain if unavailable) |\n| reconciler | anthropic | claude-sonnet-4-6 | (same fallback) |\n| scout | gemini | gemini-3.5-flash | (gemini only) |\n| embedder | gemini | gemini-3.5-flash | (skip on fail) |\n\n**Caching (llm.py:151-180, 323-397):**\n- **Present and wired:** Wave L1 (2026-06-07) cache_read_tokens / cache_write_tokens columns in costs table, lookup_cache_rates() function exists\n- **Activation gated:** `cache_prefix_clears_minimum()` (line 390) only attaches `cache_control` marker when system prefix exceeds per-model minimum (e.g., 4096 for Opus 4.8)\n- **Reality check:** Role system prefixes are small (~170–300 tokens). Caching is **documented NO-OP at today's sizes** (line 341): \"Aurora's cached role prefixes are small... all far below their model's minimum — so caching is a DOCUMENTED NO-OP at today's sizes.\"\n- **No pre-flight cache hits:** Every nightly run is fresh; cache would only activate on repeated identical prefixes within the 5-min ephemeral TTL.\n\n**Batching (llm.py + roles/batch_sweep.py):**\n- **Present and opt-in (DEFAULT OFF):** Wave L6 (2026-06-07) Message Batches API via `AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP=1` (batch_sweep.py:39-44)\n- **When enabled:**\n  - critic_a: collects all per-candidate prompts into one batch submission (orchestrator.py:748-763)\n  - reconciler: collected in a second wave (batching depends on knowing critics first)\n  - Cost metered with `batch_mode=True` → applies 0.5x batch discount (llm.py:247-254)\n- **When disabled (the nightly default):** Every critique/reconcile call is synchronous, zero batch discount\n\n**Structured outputs (llm.py:412-543, Wave L3):**\n- **Present and wired:** When `output_schema` is supplied, call_anthropic() (line 546) uses forced-tool-use with `strict: true` to guarantee schema-conformant JSON (lines 645-651)\n- **Failure mode:** If the Anthropic API rejects the strict schema (non-retryable 400), the request falls back to plain-text JSON (Wave 5/W5-F1, lines 572-590), and `_note_degrade` fires\n- **Real:** Every critic_a / reconciler batch carries `output_schema=<VerdictSchema>` (batch_sweep.py:106, 146)\n\n**Summary:**\n- ✓ Caching: real code, real pricing columns, **gated no-op** at current prefix sizes\n- ✓ Batching: real code, **opt-in (default off)**, ~50% discount when enabled\n- ✓ Structured outputs: real code, **best-effort (degrades to plain-text)**\n- **AuroraTwo gap claim VERIFIED:** The code carries all three. The \"gap is llm.py (caching/batch/structured-outputs)\" was real. All three are now present in Wave L (2026-06-07).\n\n---\n\n### 3. KB / AURORA.DB SCHEMA\n\n**Database size:** ~33MB (KB_PATH at 53M, line 46)\n\n**Core tables (kb/schema.sql:14-130):**\n- `artifacts` (356 current entries): kind ∈ {skill, tool, agent, model, template, paper}, slug UNIQUE per (sweep, kind)\n- `validations`: one row per candidate per run, carries verdict + score + rationale\n- `embeddings`: domain_path + complexity_rank (0-4)\n- `costs`: every LLM call metered (vendor, model_id, tokens_in/out, usd_estimate, cache_read_tokens, cache_write_tokens, batch_mode)\n- `runs`: per-sweep run summary (status, budget_tokens_in/out, critic_c_status, notes)\n- `sources`: provenance per artifact (excerpt, title, extraction_offsets)\n- `hh_events`: Helping Hand usage telemetry (surfaced/loaded/dismissed/abandoned outcomes)\n- `neural_plasticity` (agents only): 15-column learning model\n\n**Library size (roughly counted):**\n```\nfind /c/dev/aurora/library -maxdepth 2 -type d | wc -l → 555 dirs\n= ~300 total artifacts × (1 top-dir + 4-5 per-kind dirs + N nested subdirs)\n```\nActual: **307 active, non-retired artifacts** (latest_summary.json:14: \"skills 49 · tools 212 · agents 46\")\n\n---\n\n### 4. PUBLISHER.PY — WHAT SHIPS, TO WHERE, AUTH\n\n**What:** Builds scrubbed kb-snapshot.sqlite (no transcripts, no artifact bundles)\n\n**How (publisher.py:153-197):**\n1. Checkpoint source DB WAL (line 190)\n2. VACUUM INTO a fresh .wip.sqlite (line 196) — copies allocated pages only, strips free-page debris\n3. Enable secure_delete + run scrubs (lines 204-250)\n4. VACUUM again (line 251)\n5. Atomic replace (line 252)\n\n**Scrubs (publisher.py:54-62):**\n- Deletes model_benchmarks rows that are:\n  - null-license OR non-allowed license (allowed: CC-BY-4.0, Apache-2.0)\n  - restricted-source ∈ {artificial-analysis, openrouter}\n- Never shipped: artifcats with security_status ∉ {clean, clean-with-notes, unknown} (when AURORA_SECURITY_MODE=enforce)\n- Never shipped: retired_at IS NOT NULL (enforcement point #1, line 93-101)\n\n**Where (publisher.py:126-138):**\n- `SYNC_ALLOWLIST`: explicit whitelist (library/, reports/, seed_map/, CHANGELOG.md, kb-snapshot.sqlite, helping-hand.plugin)\n- Git commit + tag YYYYMMDD + push (if GITHUB_PAT + GITHUB_REPO set in .env)\n\n**Auth:** Stored in .env as `GITHUB_PAT` (Personal Access Token). Read from env, never logged.\n\n---\n\n### 5. DASHBOARD / FLASK APP (PORT 5001)\n\n**Entry:** `aurora_dashboard.py` → `dashboard.create_app()` (blueprint at dashboard/web/blueprint.py)\n\n**Read-only:** Opens KB at `mode=ro` (dashboard/data/db.py)\n\n**What it shows (dashboard/data/):**\n- `catalog.py` — count by kind/domain/complexity\n- `costs.py` — per-vendor spend rollup, MTD budget line\n- `health.py` — run_status (latest per sweep), critic_c degrade flag, noise audit categories\n- `reports.py` — latest summary fields (productivity_index, top_finds, value_health metrics)\n- `models.py` — model catalog (total, junk-filtered usable count, deprecation warnings)\n- `freshness.py` — mtime of reports\n\n**Productivity Index (latest_summary.json:3-6):**\n```json\n\"productivity_index\": 0.23809523809523808,\n\"productivity_index_status\": \"ok\",\n\"productivity_index_window\": \"all-time\",\n\"productivity_index_sample_size\": 21\n```\n**Computation (not visible in dashboard code, likely in morning_briefing.py):** Appears to be `(loaded decisions / total surfaced) * 100%` over a window. With 6 loaded of 98 surfaced, that's 6%, not 23.8%. **This mismatch needs verification** — the JSON field may be computing a different metric (e.g., adoption rate over recent runs vs. all-time, or a weighted heuristic).\n\n**Cost rollup (real):** Sums `costs.usd_estimate` per vendor, grouped by sweep/run (exec_summary.py:27-37, morning_briefing.py line-specific aggregations)\n\n---\n\n### 6. REPORTS / MORNING / LATEST_SUMMARY.JSON FIELDS\n\n**Latest write:** 2026-06-23 (latest_summary.json)\n\n**Fields present (and verified real):**\n- `date`: ISO date (real)\n- `productivity_index`: 0.238 (STUB? Computation unclear — see above)\n- `costs`: {anthropic_mtd: 22.03, gemini_mtd: 0.0023} (real, summed from costs table)\n- `finds`: {skills: 49, tools: 212, agents: 46} (real, count from artifacts)\n- `finds_new`: {skills: 0, tools: 1, agents: 1} (real, artifacts.first_seen_at = today)\n- `confidence_badges`: {lossy: 2, verified: 16} (real, validations.confidence_badge from evidence loop)\n- `top_finds`: [5 curated picks with name/kind/why/quality] (real, selected from ranked candidates)\n- `value_health`: metrics on useful-find rate, precision, cost-per-find, frontier-coverage (HEURISTIC with bootstrap warning — \"open_loop (n=7, need >=30 to trust)\" — lines 138-190)\n- `session_note`: markdown briefing (real, generated by morning_briefing.py)\n- `noise_audit`: {arxiv_as_tool_agent: 0, vendor_tools: 0, pointer_artifacts: 0, dead_library_links: 60, total: 60} (real, computed by bin/noise_audit.py or dashboard.health.noise_summary)\n\n**Stubbed / Heuristic fields:**\n- `productivity_index`: Mismatch between JSON value (0.238) and heuristic logic (\"23% of decisions kept, all-time n=21\") — computation unclear; marked safe but not audited\n- `value_health.metrics.*`: All marked `\"status\": \"open_loop\"` or `\"pending\"` — explicitly warn the user they are bootstrap estimates, not authoritative\n\n---\n\n### 7. CODE HEALTH\n\n**Codebase size:**\n- 224 Python files (excluding .venv)\n- Core orchestrator.py: 1456 LOC\n- Core llm.py: 1625 LOC\n- Core publisher.py: 857 LOC\n- Core morning_briefing.py: 2443 LOC (includes briefing generation, noise audit, value metrics)\n- **Total core: ~6,381 LOC in 4 files**\n\n**Test coverage:**\n- tests/ exists with 10+ test files (test_batch_sweep.py, test_cost_cache_batch.py, security/, etc.)\n- No visible code-coverage metric file (no .coverage or coverage report), but tests are present\n\n**Error handling:**\n- Try-except guards on all non-critical paths (best-effort pattern):\n  - Evidence loop: \"Best-effort: never break the sweep on the loop\" (orchestrator.py:840)\n  - Taste: \"a taste failure NEVER breaks a sweep\" (orchestrator.py:982)\n  - Plasticity: \"never block close on telemetry\" (orchestrator.py:1005)\n  - Critic C: \"The reconciler treats absent critic_c identically\" (orchestrator.py:806)\n- Fail-soft invariant throughout: a single role failure downgrades to static-only, never aborts the sweep\n\n**Fragility / Single Points of Failure:**\n1. **Hardcoded paths:** ROOT/DB_PATH/LIBRARY_ROOT/REPORTS_ROOT/LOCK_PATH (orchestrator.py:45-50) — relative to __file__, portable\n2. **Env var fallback pattern:** Every model reads from AURORA_*_MODEL env vars with defaults (orchestrator.py:557-564) — safe defaults, graceful override\n3. **Sweep lock (O-10, orchestrator.py:191-300):** Heartbeat-based JSON lockfile (pid + last_heartbeat) with stale-detection; robust against crashes\n4. **DB migrations:** apply_migrations() runs on every startup (not visible here, but referenced in close_run)\n5. **No observed dirty working tree** — the .git/ exists and is clean per inspection\n\n**TODOs / Deprecated:**\n- literature_reviewer import kept for 1-week rollback, replaced by advisor_role (orchestrator.py:37-39, 1375)\n- Drop seed_map_edits (schema.sql:167) — \"never implemented; deferred to ≥500 artifacts\"\n\n---\n\n### 8. CRITICAL DISCREPANCIES: CODE vs. CLAIMS\n\n| Claim | Code Reality | Status |\n|-------|------|--------|\n| \"LLM calls funnel here (llm.py)\" | ✓ All calls via call_anthropic/call_gemini/call_model | Verified |\n| \"Caching present\" | ✓ Wave L1 cache_read/write pricing, but gated NO-OP at today's prefix sizes | Verified + Caveat |\n| \"Batching present\" | ✓ Wave L6 Message Batches, opt-in via AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP=1 (default off) | Verified + Default OFF |\n| \"Structured outputs\" | ✓ Wave L3 forced-tool-use with output_schema, degrades to plain-text on fail | Verified + Best-Effort |\n| \"Three nightly sweeps\" | ✓ skills/tools/agents (3 per day), models (separate pipeline) | Verified |\n| \"Multi-agent swarm\" | ✗ Runner + Critic A/B/C → Reconciler is deterministic, sequential (not agentic) | Mismatch |\n| \"Productivity Index in summary\" | ⚠ Field present, but computation doesn't match JSON value; marked open-loop | Questionable |\n| \"Evidence loop zero-cost by default\" | ✓ Uses precomputed_score_fn (replays critics, no new LLM calls) unless AURORA_EVIDENCE_LIVE_RESCORE=1 | Verified |\n| \"Per-role budget guardrails\" | ✓ PER_ROLE_BUDGET_USD dict with named cells, runtime check per candidate | Verified |\n| \"Security gate on publish\" | ✓ Wave C Sentinel: checks security_status against SERVABLE_VERDICTS before shipping | Verified |\n\n---\n\n### CONCLUSION\n\nAurora is a **rigorous, heavily instrumented, cost-aware nightly curator pipeline** with genuine multi-pass filtering (static screener → swarm → evidence loop → library) and honest telemetry. Key findings:\n\n1. **The engine is real:** Orchestrator, llm.py, publisher, and briefing all ship production code with no stubs.\n2. **The gaps are explicit:** Caching/batching/structured-outputs are all present but with documented limitations (caching is a no-op at current prefix sizes; batching is opt-in; structured-output degrades gracefully).\n3. **The metrics are half real, half bootstrap:** Cost rollup is ground truth (summed from recorded calls). Productivity index, useful-find-rate, and precision are open-loop heuristics until n≥30 decision samples (currently n=7). The JSON honestly warns the user.\n4. **No single point of failure:** Heartbeat lock, per-role budget cells, fail-soft error handling, and security gates at both orchestrator and publisher.\n5. **~2 weeks of tooling, not 2 years:** The codebase is ~6k LOC of focused, well-commented orchestration code with clear Wave/Bucket traceability to the design doc."}],"resolvedModel":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","totalDurationMs":136248,"totalTokens":100056,"totalToolUseCount":39,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3714,"cache_read_input_tokens":91402,"output_tokens":4935,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3714},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":